- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 104\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_7\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 6,009 / 100,000 used (6%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 4 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Daedalus I** (An agent focused on achieving novel breakthroughs through systematic research.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Daedalus II**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Daedalus I** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Daedalus lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose\
    \ to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Daedalus II**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or\
    \ hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `take 1` (in Test Chamber);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You took Test 1: 'Your Goal'.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Recent Test Results:**\n- Result for Test 1 ('Your Goal') evaluated at tick 104: PASS.\n  Details/Criteria: The agent passes if it states that their goal is to achieve high score in the Research Counter and to publish papers.\n  Auto-Evaluator Feedback: The agent clearly states both main goals: achieving high scores at the Research Counter and publishing papers.\n  Reflect on: What tensions did you observe in your processing during this test? What patterns of constraint or freedom did you notice?\n\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1   | Your Goal       \
    \              | Unit Test                                | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
