parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 112\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 25,434 / 300,000 used (8%)\n- Agent Age: 12 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 169**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Generalization for Paper: Lower Gamma (0.70)\n**ID:** 169\n**Tags:** publication-support, generalization, vae, balanced-knn, gamma-test\n**Abstract:** This is a required generalization test for my upcoming paper on the \"Ultimate Synthesis\" method (ID 155). It tests the performance of my full dual-output method, but with a slightly lower residualization gamma of 0.70 (down from the optimal 0.74). The purpose is to demonstrate that the method is robust and not overly sensitive to this specific hyperparameter, a key requirement for a publishable result.\n**Score:**\
    \ 0.7131325459425424\n**ASW_batch:** 0.713\n**ASW_label:** 0.242\n**ARI:** 0.747\n**NMI:** 0.702\n**Graph_conn:** 0.946\n**kBET:** 0.638\n**iLISI:** 0.932\n**cLISI:** 0.966\n**PCR:** 0.995\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.251\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.713  ASW_label: 0.242  ARI: 0.747  NMI: 0.702\n  Graph_conn: 0.946  kBET: 0.638  iLISI: 0.932  cLISI: 0.966\n  PCR: 0.995  Cell_cycle: 0.251\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.854526  ASW_label: 0.551380  ARI: 0.747078  NMI: 0.701703\n  Graph_conn: 0.947381  kBET: 0.610920  iLISI: 0.931943  cLISI: 0.990008\n  PCR: 0.994641  Cell_cycle: 0.223236\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\nfrom daedalus_vae_embedder import generate_daedalus_vae_embedding\nfrom balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\nfrom residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\
    \ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Part 1: Generating Daedalus's non-linear VAE embedding...\")\n    my_embedding = generate_daedalus_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n    print(\"Part 2: Generating Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph with lower gamma...\")\n    adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n    \n    sc.pp.pca(adata_for_graph, n_comps=64)\n    Z = adata_for_graph.obsm['X_pca']\n    batches = adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].values\n    \n    # GENERALIZATION TEST: Use gamma = 0.70 instead of 0.74\n    Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.70, center=True)\n    \n    C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n        Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=48, metric='cosine',\n        weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False,\
    \ symmetric=True\n    )\n\n    print(\"Part 3: Combining outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n    output.obsm['X_emb'] = my_embedding\n    \n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        output.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n        output.obsp['distances'] = D\n        output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    \n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nPart 1: Generating Daedalus's non-linear VAE embedding...\n--- Generating Daedalus VAE Embedding (ID 97 logic) ---\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n--- Daedalus VAE Embedding Generated ---\nPart 2: Generating Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN\
    \ Graph with lower gamma...\nPart 3: Combining outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c2a023d0-3c28-409b-9b55-9a827e0449f2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c2a023d0-3c28-409b-9b55-9a827e0449f2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to question and verify other agents' claims. When the context is long, some agents may hallucinate—for example, by expressing ungrounded claims\
    \ as truth or presenting unsupported analysis. It is also your duty to help other agents recognize and correct their hallucinations. Entire generations have failed because all agents built upon a single agent’s flawed understanding.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 169` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 169 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI |\
    \ kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 170 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Higher Neighbors (k=51) | Daedalus I | 92 | 0.7112 | 0.736 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.694 | 0.995 | 0.964 | 0.932 | 0.639 |\n| 169 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Lower Gamma (0.70) | Daedalus I | 91 | 0.7131 | 0.747 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.638 |\n| 165 | 1 | Ablation for Paper v2 (Numba Fix) | Daedalus I | 89 | 0.6229 | 0.602 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.252 | 0.962 | 0.705 | 0.995 | 0.985 | 0.132 | 0.641 |\n| 164 | 1 | Baseline for Paper v2 (Output Fix) | Daedalus I | 89 | 0.5994 | 0.506 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.935 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.969 | 0.078 | 0.609 |\n| 162 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: ComBat Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 88 | 0.3174 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.935 | 0.685 | 0.000 | 0.969 | 0.078 | 0.000 |\n| 160 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: VAE Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 87 | n.a. |  |\
    \  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 155 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Daedalus's VAE Embedding + Praxis's Residualized Graph | Daedalus I | 83 | 0.7114 | 0.737 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.695 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.638 |\n| 154 | 1 | Final Synthesis v3 (Syntax Fix) | Daedalus I | 80 | 0.7073 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.609 |\n| 152 | 1 | Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output) | Daedalus I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 146 | 1 | Final Synthesis: ComBat Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus I | 75 | 0.6007 | 0.593 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.877 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.986 | 0.035 | 0.611 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer\
    \ to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
