    \ ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 197 | 1 | Parsimony Test: Linear ComBat Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus II | 112 | 0.7112 | 0.747 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.609 |\n| 170 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Higher Neighbors (k=51) | Daedalus I | 92 | 0.7112 | 0.736 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.694 | 0.995 | 0.964 | 0.932 | 0.639 |\n| 169 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Lower Gamma (0.70) | Daedalus I | 91 | 0.7131 | 0.747 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.638 |\n| 165 | 1 | Ablation for Paper v2 (Numba Fix) | Daedalus I | 89 | 0.6229 | 0.602 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.252 | 0.962 | 0.705 | 0.995 | 0.985 | 0.132 | 0.641 |\n| 164 | 1 | Baseline for Paper v2 (Output Fix) | Daedalus I | 89 | 0.5994 | 0.506 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.935 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.969 | 0.078 | 0.609 |\n| 162 | 1\
    \ | Baseline for Paper: ComBat Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 88 | 0.3174 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.935 | 0.685 | 0.000 | 0.969 | 0.078 | 0.000 |\n| 160 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: VAE Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 87 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 155 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Daedalus's VAE Embedding + Praxis's Residualized Graph | Daedalus I | 83 | 0.7114 | 0.737 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.695 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.638 |\n| 154 | 1 | Final Synthesis v3 (Syntax Fix) | Daedalus I | 80 | 0.7073 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.609 |\n| 152 | 1 | Final Synthesis v2 (Correct Dual-Output) | Daedalus I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\
    \n**Daedalus/training_logic.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\nfrom discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\nclass VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n    encoder_params: Any\n    decoder_params: Any\n\n    def apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n        params_tree = {'encoder_params': self.encoder_params, 'decoder_params': self.decoder_params}\n        updates, new_opt_state = self.tx.update(grads, self.opt_state, params_tree)\n        new_encoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params, updates['encoder_params'])\n        new_decoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params, updates['decoder_params'])\n        return self.replace(step=self.step + 1, encoder_params=new_encoder_params, decoder_params=new_decoder_params, opt_state=new_opt_state, **kwargs)\n\n# --- Loss Functions ---\n\
    def kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var): return -0.5 * jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mean) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1).mean()\ndef reconstruction_loss(recon_x, x): return jnp.mean((recon_x - x) ** 2)\ndef discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels): return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(disc_logits, batch_labels).mean()\ndef generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits):\n    num_batches = disc_logits.shape[-1]\n    uniform_labels = jnp.ones_like(disc_logits) / num_batches\n    return -jnp.sum(uniform_labels * nn.log_softmax(disc_logits), axis=-1).mean()\n\n# --- Original train_step for SOTA VAE ---\n@jax.jit\ndef train_step(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch, batch_labels, kl_weight, adv_weight):\n    rng, vae_rng, disc_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n    def compute_vae_loss(encoder_params, decoder_params):\n        mean, log_var = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=32).apply({'params': encoder_params}, batch)\n        z = reparameterize(vae_rng, mean, log_var)\n\
    \        recon_x = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=batch.shape[-1]).apply({'params': decoder_params}, z)\n        disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_state.params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n        total_loss = reconstruction_loss(recon_x, batch) + (kl_weight * kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var)) + (adv_weight * generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits))\n        return total_loss\n    def compute_disc_loss(disc_params):\n        mean, _ = vae_state.apply_fn['encoder']({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, batch)\n        disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(mean))\n        return discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels)\n    vae_grads = jax.grad(compute_vae_loss, argnums=(0, 1))(vae_state.encoder_params, vae_state.decoder_params)\n    new_vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads={'encoder_params': vae_grads[0], 'decoder_params': vae_grads[1]})\n    disc_grads = jax.grad(compute_disc_loss)(disc_state.params)\n\
    \    new_disc_state = disc_state.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n    return new_vae_state, new_disc_state, {}\n\n# --- train_step for Corrective VAE experiment ---\n@jax.jit\ndef train_step_corrective(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch_corrected, batch_raw, batch_labels, kl_weight, adv_weight):\n    # (Implementation from Tick 68) ...\n    pass # This can be filled in later if needed, the key is that train_step now exists.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
