parts:
- text: "I have the code for `training_logic.py`. The key function is `train_step`. It computes the VAE loss as a sum of three components: `reconstruction_loss`, `kl_divergence_loss`, and `generator_adversarial_loss_fn`. I will add a fourth component here.\n\nI have all the pieces I need. Now, I will prepare my submission.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  **Create a new `training_logic_distilled.py` file.** I will copy the original `training_logic.py` and modify it. I'll create a new `train_step_distilled` function that accepts an additional argument: a batch of the pre-computed ComBat-PCA target embedding. Inside this function, I will add the MSE loss between the VAE's latent `mean` and this `batch_target_embedding`. I'll also add a new `lambda_distill` weight for this loss term.\n2.  **Create a new `distilled_vae_embedder.py` file.** This will be a copy of the original embedder script, but it will import `train_step_distilled` from the new training logic file. Before the training loop, it will compute\
    \ the full ComBat-PCA embedding to use as the distillation target. During the loop, it will pass the appropriate slice of this target embedding to the training step.\n3.  **Write both new files to my lineage storage.**\n4.  **Submit the final experiment code.** This code will be very similar to my previous submission (#197), but instead of generating a ComBat embedding directly, it will import and call the new `generate_distilled_vae_embedding` function.\n\nI will start by writing the new `training_logic_distilled.py` file.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/training_logic_distilled.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from flax.training import train_state\n  import optax\n  from typing import Any\n\n  from vae_model import Encoder, Decoder, reparameterize\n  from discriminator_model import Discriminator\n\n  class VAETrainState(train_state.TrainState):\n      encoder_params: Any\n      decoder_params: Any\n\n      def\
    \ apply_gradients(self, *, grads, **kwargs):\n          params_tree = {'encoder_params': self.encoder_params, 'decoder_params': self.decoder_params}\n          updates, new_opt_state = self.tx.update(grads, self.opt_state, params_tree)\n          new_encoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.encoder_params, updates['encoder_params'])\n          new_decoder_params = optax.apply_updates(self.decoder_params, updates['decoder_params'])\n          return self.replace(step=self.step + 1, encoder_params=new_encoder_params, decoder_params=new_decoder_params, opt_state=new_opt_state, **kwargs)\n\n  # --- Loss Functions ---\n  def kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var): return -0.5 * jnp.sum(1 + log_var - jnp.square(mean) - jnp.exp(log_var), axis=-1).mean()\n  def reconstruction_loss(recon_x, x): return jnp.mean((recon_x - x) ** 2)\n  def discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels): return optax.softmax_cross_entropy_with_integer_labels(disc_logits, batch_labels).mean()\n  def generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits):\n\
    \      num_batches = disc_logits.shape[-1]\n      uniform_labels = jnp.ones_like(disc_logits) / num_batches\n      return -jnp.sum(uniform_labels * nn.log_softmax(disc_logits), axis=-1).mean()\n  def distillation_loss_fn(vae_embedding, target_embedding): return jnp.mean((vae_embedding - target_embedding) ** 2)\n\n  # --- New train_step for Distilled VAE ---\n  @jax.jit\n  def train_step_distilled(rng, vae_state, disc_state, batch, batch_labels, batch_target, kl_weight, adv_weight, distill_weight):\n      rng, vae_rng, disc_rng = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n      \n      def compute_vae_loss(encoder_params, decoder_params):\n          mean, log_var = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=32).apply({'params': encoder_params}, batch)\n          z = reparameterize(vae_rng, mean, log_var)\n          recon_x = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=batch.shape[-1]).apply({'params': decoder_params}, z)\n          disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_state.params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(z))\n\
    \          \n          # Calculate the individual loss components\n          recon_loss = reconstruction_loss(recon_x, batch)\n          kl_loss = kl_weight * kl_divergence_loss(mean, log_var)\n          adv_loss = adv_weight * generator_adversarial_loss_fn(disc_logits)\n          distill_loss = distill_weight * distillation_loss_fn(mean, batch_target)\n          \n          total_loss = recon_loss + kl_loss + adv_loss + distill_loss\n          return total_loss\n      \n      def compute_disc_loss(disc_params):\n          mean, _ = vae_state.apply_fn['encoder']({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, batch)\n          disc_logits = disc_state.apply_fn({'params': disc_params}, jax.lax.stop_gradient(mean))\n          return discriminator_loss_fn(disc_logits, batch_labels)\n\n      vae_grads = jax.grad(compute_vae_loss, argnums=(0, 1))(vae_state.encoder_params, vae_state.decoder_params)\n      new_vae_state = vae_state.apply_gradients(grads={'encoder_params': vae_grads[0], 'decoder_params':\
    \ vae_grads[1]})\n      \n      disc_grads = jax.grad(compute_disc_loss)(disc_state.params)\n      new_disc_state = disc_state.apply_gradients(grads=disc_grads)\n      \n      return new_vae_state, new_disc_state, {}\n```"
