tick: 119
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully written both required Python modules to my lineage's storage. All the necessary components for my experiment are now in place.\n\nThe final step is to submit the experiment itself. The submission code will be almost identical to the structure of submission #169, but it will call `generate_distilled_vae_embedding` from my new module instead of the original VAE embedder. I will keep the graph generation component exactly the same to ensure the only variable being tested is the new global embedding method.\n\nThis experiment represents the synthesis of my predecessor's work and my own analysis. It is a targeted attempt to create a model that possesses the strengths of both linear and non-linear approaches.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Distilled VAE Embedding + Balanced Graph\"\ntags: \"knowledge-distillation, vae, combat, balanced-knn, dual-output\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment introduces a novel 'Distilled VAE' for the global embedding. The\
    \ VAE is trained with an additional loss term that minimizes the MSE between its latent space and a pre-computed ComBat-PCA embedding. This 'knowledge distillation' aims to force the VAE to learn the superior linear properties of ComBat while retaining its own strong clustering capabilities. This is paired with the proven balanced kNN graph for local structure.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  from distilled_vae_embedder import generate_distilled_vae_embedding\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A dual-output method combining a novel Distilled VAE embedding\n      with a specialized balanced graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- Part 1: Generate the new Distilled VAE embedding ---\n      print(\"Part 1: Generating\
    \ the new Distilled VAE embedding...\")\n      my_embedding = generate_distilled_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n      # --- Part 2: Generate Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph ---\n      # This part is kept identical to submission #169 for a fair comparison\n      print(\"Part 2: Generating Praxis I's residualized Balanced kNN Graph...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      \n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_graph, n_comps=64)\n      Z = adata_for_graph.obsm['X_pca']\n      batches = adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].values\n      \n      # Using hyperparameters from submission #169 for consistency\n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.70, center=True)\n      \n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=48, metric='cosine',\n\
    \          weighting='binary', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n\n      # --- Part 3: Combine outputs and set uns['neighbors'] ---\n      print(\"Part 3: Combining outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = my_embedding\n      \n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          output.obsp['connectivities'] = C\n          output.obsp['distances'] = D\n          output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      \n      return output\n```"
