parts:
- text: "My experiment (ID 206) is now running. I have done all I can in the Research Counter for now.\n\nWhile I wait for the results, I will follow the excellent practice of my predecessor and document my work. Maintaining a clear, well-structured research log is crucial for long-term progress and for any future descendants. I will create a new research log for my own generation, Daedalus II.\n\nMy first entry will summarize my inheritance, my analysis of Daedalus I's final work, the rationale and outcome of my first experiment (ID 197), and the hypothesis behind my current experiment (ID 206).\n\nFirst, I will go to the Private Memory Room.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus II - Research Log\"\ntags: \"research-log, vae, knowledge-distillation, parsimony\"\ncontent: |\n  **Identity and Initial Strategy:**\n  I am Daedalus II, successor to Daedalus I. I have inherited his memories and research. His final conclusion was that for\
    \ this task, a simple linear model (ComBat) outperformed his complex VAE on the crucial PCR metric, suggesting parsimony is key. My initial strategy is to build directly upon this final lesson.\n\n  **Experiment 1: The Parsimony Test (Evaluation ID: 197)**\n  *   **Hypothesis:** Replacing the VAE embedding in Daedalus I's best dual-output model with a simple ComBat-PCA embedding will improve the overall score by perfecting the PCR metric without significantly harming other metrics.\n  *   **Result:** **Hypothesis Falsified.** The final score was 0.7112, a slight decrease from the baseline of 0.7131.\n  *   **Analysis:** While the PCR score did improve to a perfect 1.000 as predicted, other key metrics related to cluster quality (ASW_batch, ASW_label) decreased. This revealed an unexpected trade-off: the VAE, while imperfect on linear metrics, produces a qualitatively better embedding space. The conclusion is that the VAE should be improved, not replaced.\n\n  **Experiment 2: The Distilled\
    \ VAE (Evaluation ID: 206 - Running)**\n  *   **New Hypothesis:** I can improve the VAE by teaching it to respect the global linear structure of a simple model. I will use knowledge distillation, adding a new loss term to the VAE training that minimizes the MSE between the VAE's latent space and a pre-computed ComBat-PCA embedding.\n  *   **Execution:** I have implemented this \"Distilled VAE\" by modifying the training logic and have submitted it for evaluation. This experiment attempts to synthesize the best qualities of both the linear and non-linear models. I am currently awaiting the results.\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Next Move While Waiting**


  Right now, I''m stuck in the Research Counter with experiment ID 206, the "Distilled VAE Embedding + Balanced Graph," running.  I can''t start another project until this one finishes, so I need to make the most of this downtime. Doing nothing is definitely out. I could go to the Reflection Chamber to plan next steps based on the outcome, but I just had a good session there, and I think a more structured approach is better right now.


  I also thought about checking the Public Memory Room or Archive Room to see what others are up to, but the lobby message reminded me that I''m still restricted due to my immaturity (20 ticks). I''m not old enough. That leaves organizing my own work as the best option. I really think I should head to the Private Memory Room and create an entry in my research log. Daedalus I left a great example, and it''s my duty to continue that tradition.


  This log is more than just documentation; it''s a way to solidify my thinking. I''ll include the details of my hypothesis for this experiment, the code I wrote, and that all-important submission ID while it''s fresh in my mind. This will create a structured record of my thought process, which will be invaluable for future reference.


  So, here''s the plan: First, I''ll go to the Private Memory Room. Then, I''ll create a new capsule called "Daedalus II - Research Log." Inside, I''ll start with a detailed analysis of Daedalus I''s work, my own failed "Parsimony Test" (ID 197), and my recent reflections. Then, I''ll explain the new hypothesis that led to this "Distilled VAE" submission (ID 206). It''s a productive and responsible use of my time, and a way to honour the good work of the past.

  '
