parts:
- text: "Excellent! The results for my Distilled VAE experiment (ID 206) have arrived, and they are a resounding success.\n\n**Analysis of Submission #206:**\n\n-   **New Score:** **0.7179**\n-   **Previous Best Score (Daedalus I, ID 169):** 0.7131\n-   **Result:** **Hypothesis Confirmed.** I have achieved a new state-of-the-art score for my lineage and likely for the station.\n\n**Detailed Metric Comparison:**\n\n-   **PCR:** The distillation was a complete success. The PCR score is now 1.000, matching the perfect score of a simple linear model.\n-   **ASW Scores:** The ASW_label score (0.235) is nearly identical to the original VAE's score (0.242), indicating that I have retained the strong clustering properties. The ASW_batch score (0.604) is lower, but this trade-off was clearly worth it.\n-   **Other Metrics:** The `kBET` and `Cell_cycle` scores also improved, contributing to the overall score increase. The graph-based metrics (ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, iLISI, cLISI) are unchanged, as expected,\
    \ since the graph generation method was not altered.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nThe knowledge distillation approach worked exactly as intended. It successfully integrated the linear stability of ComBat into the VAE, fixing the PCR score while preserving the VAE's other beneficial qualities. This is a significant step forward.\n\nMy next step is to update my research log with this success and then consider how to build upon it. I could explore tuning the `distill_weight` hyperparameter, or I could investigate improvements to the graph construction component, which I have so far left untouched. Given the success of this method, I should probably try to tune it first.\n\nI will now update my research log.\n\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Experiment 2: The Distilled VAE (Evaluation ID: 206) - Results**\n  *   **Result:** **Hypothesis Confirmed & SOTA Achieved!** The final score is **0.7179**, a new high score for the lineage.\n  *   **Analysis:** The knowledge distillation\
    \ strategy was highly effective. The new model achieved a perfect PCR score of 1.000, proving it successfully learned the global linear structure from the ComBat-PCA target. Simultaneously, it maintained the strong cell type clustering performance of the original VAE (ASW_label: 0.235). This confirms that synthesizing the properties of simple and complex models within a single framework is a fruitful research direction.\n\n  **Next Steps:**\n  The `distill_weight` was set to 0.1 for the first experiment. This success warrants a follow-up experiment to see if this can be improved. I will now test a higher `distill_weight` to see if I can further improve the embedding. My next experiment will use a `distill_weight` of 0.5.\n```"
