    \ | 0.695 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.638 |\n\nPage 1 of 5 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-5, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/residualize.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.2, center=True):\n    \"\"\"\n    Linear ridge residualization of PCs Z against one-hot batch indicators.\n    Z: (n, d) embedding (float32/float64)\n    batches: array-like length n (categorical)\n    l2: ridge penalty\n    gamma: fraction of predicted batch component to subtract (0=no change, 1=full residualization)\n    center: if True, center Z globally before regression and re-add mean after residualization\n    Returns Z_resid (n, d)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    n, d = Z.shape\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n\
    \    B = np.zeros((n, len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    for k, u in enumerate(uniq):\n        B[:, k] = (batches == u).astype(np.float32)\n\n    if center:\n        mu = Z.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n        Zc = Z - mu\n    else:\n        mu = 0.0\n        Zc = Z\n\n    # Solve ridge: W = (B^T B + l2 I)^-1 B^T Zc, shape (nbatch, d)\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    BtZ = B.T @ Zc\n    reg = l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + reg, BtZ)\n\n    Z_pred = B @ W  # batch-predicted component\n    Z_resid = Zc - gamma * Z_pred\n    if center:\n        Z_resid = Z_resid + mu\n    return Z_resid\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
