tick: 132
role: model
parts:
- text: "My log is updated with the failure of my last experiment and the hypothesis for my next one.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement and submit my new experiment. I will change the `weighting` parameter in the `build_balanced_knn` call from `'binary'` to `'gaussian'`, while keeping all other parameters at their optimal values (including `allocation='equal'`).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Graph Tuning: Gaussian Weighting\"\ntags: \"graph-construction, balanced-knn, hyperparameter-tuning, gaussian-weighting\"\nabstract: |\n  Following a failed experiment with 'proportional' allocation, this submission tests another parameter in the graph construction phase. I am changing the 'weighting' from 'binary' to 'gaussian'. My hypothesis is that weighting edges by their distance will create a more nuanced local graph, potentially improving biological conservation metrics without harming the excellent batch mixing provided\
    \ by the 'equal' allocation strategy.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n\n  from distilled_vae_embedder import generate_distilled_vae_embedding\n  from balanced_graph import build_balanced_knn\n  from residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A dual-output method testing a modification to the graph construction.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- Part 1: Generate the SOTA Distilled VAE embedding ---\n      print(\"Part 1: Generating the SOTA Distilled VAE embedding...\")\n      my_embedding = generate_distilled_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n      # --- Part 2: Generate Praxis I's graph with a modification ---\n      print(\"Part 2: Generating Balanced kNN Graph with GAUSSIAN weighting...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n\
    \      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_graph, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n      \n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_graph, n_comps=64)\n      Z = adata_for_graph.obsm['X_pca']\n      batches = adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].values\n      \n      Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma=0.70, center=True)\n      \n      # HYPOTHESIS TEST: Change weighting from 'binary' to 'gaussian'\n      C, D = build_balanced_knn(\n          Z_resid, batches, n_neighbors_total=48, metric='cosine',\n          weighting='gaussian', allocation='equal', mutual=False, symmetric=True\n      )\n\n      # --- Part 3: Combine outputs and set uns['neighbors'] ---\n      print(\"Part 3: Combining outputs and setting uns['neighbors']...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = my_embedding\n      \n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          output.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = C\n          output.obsp['distances'] = D\n          output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      \n      return output\n```"
