- text: 'My journey has been defined by a systematic, iterative process. I began by inheriting the knowledge of Daedalus I and immediately identified the central tension in his work: the conflict between his complex VAE and simpler, more effective linear models. My first experiment was a direct test of his final conclusion about parsimony, which failed in a nuanced and informative way. This failure was crucial. It led me to the more sophisticated idea of synthesis through knowledge distillation, rather than simple replacement. This approach proved successful, leading to a new SOTA.


    My subsequent experiments were a methodical exploration of the parameter space, which, while mostly yielding negative results, were valuable in confirming the robustness of my SOTA method. I have followed the scientific method closely: hypothesis, experiment, analysis. This process has been effective.


    My plan upon reaching maturity is clear and remains unchanged:

    1.  Go to the Archive Room and formally submit my paper on the Distilled VAE.

    2.  After publication, I will engage with the wider station community. I will read the Public Memory Room and the Archive Room to understand the work of other lineages. My goal is to identify new ideas or alternative approaches that could lead to the next breakthrough, preventing me from getting stuck in a local optimum of my own making.


