parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 154\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,349 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 54 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 12 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment\
    \ delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `storage read praxis/best_dual_brbg_whitened.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for praxis/best_dual_brbg_whitened.py will be\
    \ displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding\
    \ (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 251 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Auto-τ Whitening + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 150 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 235 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.97) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.075 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 234 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.93) + Equal-Quota\
    \ Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.078 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 224 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.7) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 131 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.827 | 0.181 | 0.123 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.844 |\n| 243 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=51, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7286 | 0.735 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.078 | 0.972 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.932 | 0.905 |\n\nPage 1 of 26 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-26, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**praxis/best_dual_brbg_whitened.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\
    \ _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn_equal\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n    var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n    if var is None:\n        return Z\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    return Zw - Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dual BRBG (adaptive residualized graph PCs + equal-quotas BalancedGraph)\n    with ComBat-PCA64 embedding + PCA-axis whitening (tau=0.95).\n    Final defaults (EID 244 = 0.7296): k_total=45, cosine.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config (frozen)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 45            # updated from 48 → 45 per\
    \ EID 244 (SOTA 0.7296)\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    tau_whiten = 0.95\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize + HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3',\n                                batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph view: PCs + adaptive residualization vs batch\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr,\
    \ batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding view: ComBat + PCA64 + whitening (tau=0.95)\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True,\n              svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=tau_whiten, eps=1e-8)\n\n    # Output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_whiten'] = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'tau_whiten':\
    \ float(tau_whiten),\n        'notes': 'EID 244 (k=45) = 0.7296; UUID 3fc52313-69ec-4a0a-8b75-6dd8c489eb0c'\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 154
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received another inactivity notice. I must act swiftly.\n\nI have read the SOTA script from Praxis I. The key function is `_whiten_pcs`. It takes a PCA embedding, retrieves the variance of each PC, and then rescales each PC axis. It divides by the standard deviation (sqrt of variance) and multiplies by a factor `tau`. This makes the variance along each axis equal, effectively making the data distribution more spherical or \"isotropic\".\n\n**My Synthesis Plan is now concrete:**\n\n1.  **Generate my Distilled VAE embedding:** I will use my established method to create the `X_emb` from my SOTA experiment (ID 213).\n2.  **Apply Whitening:** I will take this DVAE embedding and apply Praxis I's whitening function to it. This will require a slight modification. The original `_whiten_pcs` function relies on the `adata.uns['pca']['variance']` which is populated by `sc.pp.pca`. My DVAE embedding doesn't come from `sc.pp.pca`, so this won't exist. I will have to compute the variance\
    \ of each dimension of my DVAE embedding manually and then apply the same scaling logic.\n3.  **Use the SOTA Graph:** I will use the rest of Praxis I's script verbatim to generate the graph component. Their paper indicates they have optimized this part thoroughly (e.g., adaptive residualization, `k=45`). There is no reason to deviate from it.\n\nThis experiment directly tests the synergy between my novel embedding and their novel post-processing step. It is the most promising path to a new SOTA and will resolve my inactivity status.\n\nI will now create a new script in my storage to encapsulate this logic, then submit the experiment.\n\n/execute_action{storage write Daedalus/synthesized_whitened_dvae.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n\n  # Import my DVAE embedder\n  from distilled_vae_embedder import\
    \ generate_distilled_vae_embedding\n\n  # Import Praxis I's graph utilities and SOTA graph construction logic\n  from praxis.brbg_common import (\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n      _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn_equal\n  )\n\n  def whiten_embedding(embedding, tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies PCA-axis whitening to a pre-computed embedding.\n      Modified from Praxis I's work to not depend on an AnnData object.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Manually compute variance for each dimension of the embedding\n      variances = np.var(embedding, axis=0)\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(variances, eps, None))\n      \n      # Apply whitening\n      whitened_embedding = (embedding / scale) * float(tau)\n      return whitened_embedding - whitened_embedding.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A synthesis of my Distilled VAE embedding and Praxis\
    \ I's whitening.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- Part 1: Generate my SOTA Distilled VAE embedding ---\n      print(\"Part 1: Generating the SOTA Distilled VAE embedding...\")\n      dvae_embedding = generate_distilled_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n      # --- Part 2: Apply Praxis I's whitening to the DVAE embedding ---\n      print(\"Part 2: Applying whitening to the DVAE embedding...\")\n      tau_whiten = 0.95\n      whitened_dvae_embedding = whiten_embedding(dvae_embedding, tau=tau_whiten)\n\n      # --- Part 3: Generate Praxis I's SOTA Graph ---\n      print(\"Part 3: Generating Praxis I's SOTA graph...\")\n      # This logic is taken directly from praxis/best_dual_brbg_whitened.py\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n      \n      adata_graph = adata.copy()\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph, n_top_genes=2000,\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3',\n                                  batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata_graph.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      Xg = adata_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Part 4: Combine outputs ---\n      print(\"Part 4: Combining outputs...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = whitened_dvae_embedding\n      \n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n\
    \          output.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          output.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return output\n```"
