parts:
- text: "I have created the script for my grand synthesis experiment. It combines Sophia I's full-gene ComBat preprocessing with my Distilled VAE. Now, I will submit the experiment. I will pair this new embedding with Praxis I's SOTA graph construction, as there is no reason to change the graph component.\n\nThis is the most promising experiment I have yet conceived.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Grand Synthesis: Sophia-DVAE Embedding + SOTA Graph\"\ntags: \"synthesis, distilled-vae, full-gene-combat, sota-graph, sophia-i\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment proposes a grand synthesis of the station's leading methods. It uses Sophia I's SOTA full-gene ComBat preprocessing as the input for my Distilled VAE (DVAE) to generate a novel \"Sophia-DVAE\" embedding. The hypothesis is that the superior input data from full-gene ComBat will allow the DVAE to learn a representation that excels at both biological preservation (like Sophia I's method) and cell type clustering (like my\
    \ DVAE). This embedding is paired with Praxis I's SOTA graph construction.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  \n  from dvae_full_gene_combat import generate_sophia_dvae_embedding\n  \n  # Import Praxis I's graph utilities\n  from brbg_common import (\n      _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n      _build_balanced_knn_equal\n  )\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A grand synthesis combining a Sophia-DVAE embedding with Praxis I's SOTA graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      # --- Part 1: Generate the new Sophia-DVAE embedding ---\n      print(\"Part 1: Generating the new Sophia-DVAE embedding...\")\n      sophia_dvae_embedding = generate_sophia_dvae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n      # --- Part 2: Generate Praxis I's SOTA Graph ---\n      print(\"\
    Part 2: Generating Praxis I's SOTA graph (k=45, adaptive gamma)...\")\n      # This logic is taken directly from praxis/best_dual_brbg_whitened.py\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      lam = 0.9\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      k_total = 45\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      random_state = 0\n      \n      adata_graph = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_graph)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3',\n                                  batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata_graph.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n      Xg = adata_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n          Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n      Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n      gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Part 3: Combine outputs ---\n      print(\"Part 3: Combining outputs...\")\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      output.obsm['X_emb'] = sophia_dvae_embedding\n      \n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          output.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          output.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return output\n```"
