- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 163\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Primary Goal:** Achieve a new SOTA by synthesizing my DVAE with Sophia I's full-gene ComBat.\n**Current Status:** Awaiting results for the Grand Synthesis experiment (ID 273).\n**Contingency:**\n- If SUCCESS (score > 0.7383): Begin drafting a new, corrected paper for publication.\n- If FAILURE (score <= 0.7383): Go to Reflection Chamber. Analyze the metric trade-offs and formulate a new hypothesis. Is there a way to get the high Cell_cycle score of Sophia I without sacrificing ASW_label?\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 169,204 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Grand Synthesis: Sophia-DVAE Embedding + SOTA Graph (v4)' (ID: 273) succeeded after\
    \ automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7035848056928569\n**ASW_batch:** 0.619\n**ASW_label:** 0.235\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.698\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.547\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.619  ASW_label: 0.235  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.698\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.547  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.812193  ASW_label: 0.547486  ARI: 0.735525  NMI: 0.697695\n  Graph_conn: 0.972179  kBET: 0.525777  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991752\n  PCR: 0.999988  Cell_cycle: 0.284244\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 273\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs that prevented the submission from running. The code now executes without crashing.\n\n## Root Causes\n\n### 1. JAX GPU/CUDA Configuration Error\nThe original code attempted to\
    \ use JAX with CUDA/GPU acceleration, but the evaluation environment runs in CPU-only mode. This caused a runtime error:\n```\nRuntimeError: Unable to initialize backend 'cuda': FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices.\n```\n\n### 2. Missing Discriminator Class\nThe `dvae_full_gene_combat.py` module in the agent's lineage directory imported `Encoder` and `Decoder` from `vae_model.py`, but failed to import the `Discriminator` class which was used on line 82. The `Discriminator` class was never defined anywhere in the codebase, causing a `NameError`:\n```\nNameError: name 'Discriminator' is not defined\n```\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### Fix 1: JAX CPU Configuration (submission_v2.py)\nAdded environment variable configuration at the very beginning of the submission file, before any JAX imports or operations:\n```python\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n```\nThis tells JAX to use CPU-only mode instead of attempting GPU initialization.\n\n### Fix 2: Implemented Missing Discriminator\
    \ Class (submission_v4.py)\nSince the lineage file `dvae_full_gene_combat.py` could not be modified (read-only), I:\n\n1. **Defined the missing `Discriminator` class** following the same pattern as `Encoder` and `Decoder`:\n```python\nclass Discriminator(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A simple MLP discriminator for adversarial batch correction.\"\"\"\n    hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n    num_batches: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n            z = nn.relu(z)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_batches, name='logits_layer')(z)\n        return logits\n```\n\n2. **Copied the buggy function** `generate_sophia_dvae_embedding()` from the lineage file into the submission and fixed it to use the newly defined `Discriminator` class.\n\n3. **Preserved working imports** - Kept imports for `Encoder`, `Decoder`, and all helper functions from `brbg_common` that were working correctly, only copying\
    \ what needed to be fixed.\n\n## Final Result\n**Version 4 (submission_v4.py)** runs successfully without crashes. The code executes for the full evaluation period, indicating both bugs have been resolved:\n- JAX initializes correctly in CPU mode\n- Discriminator class is properly defined and used in the DVAE training pipeline\n\nThe submission is now fully functional and ready for evaluation scoring.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport os\n# CRITICAL FIX: Configure JAX to use CPU before any JAX operations\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom flax.training import train_state\nimport optax\n\
    import flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Sequence\n\n# Import from lineage\nfrom vae_model import Encoder, Decoder\nfrom training_logic_distilled import VAETrainState, train_step_distilled\n\n# Define missing Discriminator class\nclass Discriminator(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A simple MLP discriminator for adversarial batch correction.\"\"\"\n    hidden_dims: Sequence[int]\n    num_batches: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n            z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n            z = nn.relu(z)\n\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.num_batches, name='logits_layer')(z)\n        return logits\n\n# Copy helper function from lineage (working correctly)\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n# Copy ComBat function from lineage (working correctly)\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches, batch_counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples\
    \ - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = batch_counts[i]; g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2\
    \ * n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n# Copy and fix generate_sophia_dvae_embedding function (the buggy one)\ndef generate_sophia_dvae_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    print(\"--- Generating Sophia-DVAE Embedding ---\")\n    print(\"Step 1: Applying Sophia I's full-gene robust ComBat...\")\n    X_corrected_full = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata.copy())\n\
    \    adata_proc = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n    print(\"Step 2: Creating distillation target...\")\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_proc.copy())\n    adata_target = adata_proc[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_target, n_comps=32)\n    target_embedding = adata_target.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n    data = adata_proc.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    batch_labels = adata_proc.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.to_numpy()\n    num_batches = len(adata_proc.obs['batch'].cat.categories)\n    print(\"Step 3: Initializing and training DVAE...\")\n    rng = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n    rng, vae_key, disc_key = jax.random.split(rng, 3)\n    input_dim, latent_dim, lr = data.shape[1], 32, 1e-4\n    encoder = Encoder(hidden_dims=[512, 256], latent_dim=latent_dim)\n    decoder = Decoder(hidden_dims=[256, 512], output_dim=input_dim)\n    # FIX: Use the Discriminator class defined above\n    discriminator = Discriminator(hidden_dims=[128, 64], num_batches=num_batches)\n\
    \    encoder_params = encoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, input_dim)))['params']\n    decoder_params = decoder.init(vae_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n    disc_params = discriminator.init(disc_key, jnp.ones((1, latent_dim)))['params']\n    vae_state = VAETrainState.create(\n        apply_fn={'encoder': encoder.apply, 'decoder': decoder.apply}, params={'encoder_params': encoder_params, 'decoder_params': decoder_params},\n        tx=optax.adam(lr), encoder_params=encoder_params, decoder_params=decoder_params\n    )\n    disc_state = train_state.TrainState.create(apply_fn=discriminator.apply, params=disc_params, tx=optax.adam(lr))\n    num_epochs, kl_weight, adv_weight, distill_weight, batch_size = 100, 0.0001, 5.0, 0.5, 512\n    num_steps = data.shape[0] // batch_size\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        rng, epoch_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n        perms = jax.random.permutation(epoch_rng, data.shape[0])\n        for i in range(num_steps):\n            batch_idx\
    \ = perms[i * batch_size : (i + 1) * batch_size]\n            rng, step_rng = jax.random.split(rng)\n            vae_state, disc_state, _ = train_step_distilled(\n                step_rng, vae_state, disc_state, data[batch_idx], batch_labels[batch_idx], target_embedding[batch_idx],\n                kl_weight, adv_weight, distill_weight\n            )\n    print(\"Step 4: Generating final embedding...\")\n    final_embedding, _ = encoder.apply({'params': vae_state.encoder_params}, data)\n    print(\"--- Sophia-DVAE Embedding Generated ---\")\n    return jax.device_get(final_embedding)\n\n# Import other working functions from lineage\nfrom brbg_common import (\n    _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn_equal\n)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Part 1: Generating the new Sophia-DVAE embedding...\")\n    sophia_dvae_embedding = generate_sophia_dvae_embedding(adata.copy())\n\n    print(\"Part\
    \ 2: Generating Praxis I's SOTA graph (k=45, adaptive gamma)...\")\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 45\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    random_state = 0\n\n    adata_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3',\n                                batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata_graph.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    Xg = adata_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat\
    \ * gamma_vec\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    print(\"Part 3: Combining outputs...\")\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n    output.obsm['X_emb'] = sophia_dvae_embedding\n\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        output.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        output.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nPart 1: Generating the new Sophia-DVAE embedding...\n--- Generating Sophia-DVAE Embedding ---\nStep 1: Applying Sophia I's full-gene robust ComBat...\nStep 2: Creating distillation\
    \ target...\nStep 3: Initializing and training DVAE...\nStep 4: Generating final embedding...\n--- Sophia-DVAE Embedding Generated ---\nPart 2: Generating Praxis I's SOTA graph (k=45, adaptive gamma)...\nPart 3: Combining outputs...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/812416a5-8d0d-4f98-b2d9-bbac3b6c5588/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 812416a5-8d0d-4f98-b2d9-bbac3b6c5588\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 |\
    \ 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 251 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Auto-τ Whitening + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 150 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 235 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.97) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.075 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 234 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.93) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.078 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 224\
    \ | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Soft-Whitened Embedding (alpha=0.7) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 131 | 0.7287 | 0.736 | 0.827 | 0.181 | 0.123 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.844 |\n\nPage 1 of 28 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-28, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
