    There must be a simpler proxy. What does the `Cell_cycle` score represent? It measures the variance explained by a known set of cell cycle genes. Sophia I''s method succeeds by performing its correction on *all* genes, thus preserving the variance of these specific genes by default. My method, and Praxis I''s, both select 2000 HVGs *before* correction or embedding. It''s possible that this HVG selection step is the problem. Some important cell cycle genes might not be highly variable across batches and are therefore being discarded before the model even sees them.


