- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 171\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Primary Goal:** Achieve a new SOTA by synthesizing the best linear methods from Sophia I and Praxis I.\n**Current Status:** Formulating the \"Linear Synthesis\" experiment.\n**Hypothesis:** The pipeline `Full-Gene ComBat -> HVG -> PCA -> Whitening` will combine the high `Cell_cycle` score from Sophia's preprocessing with the high mixing scores from Praxis's post-processing, yielding a new SOTA.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,064 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 71 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Veritas I** (An agent dedicated\
    \ to the pursuit of truth through rigorous experimentation and knowledge sharing.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Linear Synthesis: Sophia's Preprocessing + Praxis's Post-processing' (ID: 285) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7258466742756526\n**ASW_batch:** 0.839\n**ASW_label:** 0.157\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.698\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.872\n**iLISI:** 0.935\n**cLISI:** 0.972\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.079\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.839  ASW_label: 0.157  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.698\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.872  iLISI: 0.935  cLISI: 0.972\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.079\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.911328  ASW_label: 0.502360  ARI: 0.735525  NMI: 0.697695\n  Graph_conn: 0.972179  kBET: 0.830453  iLISI: 0.935143  cLISI: 0.991752\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.076746\n\n**Debugger Report:** #\
    \ Debug Report for Evaluation 285\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the ModuleNotFoundError by adding the missing sys.path modification. The code now runs successfully and achieved a score of 0.7258466742756526.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to import from `praxis.brbg_common` without first adding the storage directory to Python's module search path. The import statement:\n```python\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n```\n\nfailed with:\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'praxis'\n```\n\nThe `praxis` module exists at `storage/praxis/brbg_common.py` (a symlink to the lineage directory `/home/ubuntu/station/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/praxis/`), but Python couldn't find it because the storage directory wasn't in the module search path.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded two lines at the beginning of the submission (after the other imports):\n\n```python\nimport\
    \ sys\n# Add storage to path so we can import from praxis\nsys.path.append('storage')\n```\n\nThis modification allows Python to locate the `praxis` package in the storage directory, enabling the import to succeed. The rest of the code remained unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n- The fixed submission (v2) was automatically evaluated\n- Execution completed without errors\n- Final score: 0.7258466742756526\n- Monitor script exit code: 0 (success with score)\n\n## Technical Details\nThe submission combines:\n- Sophia I's robust ComBat implementation for full-gene batch correction\n- Praxis I's whitening function for embedding post-processing\n- Praxis I's SOTA graph generation method using balanced k-NN\n\nThe fix was minimal and surgical - only adding the path configuration needed for the existing logic to execute properly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged\
    \ Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n\n# Add storage to path so we can import from praxis\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\n# --- Sophia I's robust ComBat for full genes (ID 166) ---\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches, batch_counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n\
    \    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2 * s2 + m**2) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m * s2 + m**3) / (s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = batch_counts[i]; g_old,\
    \ d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2 * n * g_old + d_old * gamma_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b_prior[i]) / (n / 2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change = max(np.abs(g_new - g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new - d_old).max()); g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    X_corrected = bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean\n    return np.nan_to_num(X_corrected.T)\n\n# --- Praxis I's whitening function (ID 244) ---\ndef _whiten_pcs(Z, variance, tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(variance[:Z.shape[1]],\
    \ eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    return Zw - Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Linear Synthesis: Sophia's Preprocessing + Praxis's Post-processing...\")\n\n    # SOTA parameters from Sophia and Praxis\n    n_pcs_emb=64\n    n_pcs_graph=50\n    gamma_max=0.74\n    lam=0.9\n    l2=1e-3\n    k_total=45\n    metric='cosine'\n    tau_whiten=0.95\n    random_state = 0\n\n    # --- Embedding Path: Full-Gene ComBat -> HVG -> PCA -> Whitening ---\n    print(\"Step 1: Running Sophia's full-gene ComBat...\")\n    X_combat_full = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata.copy())\n\n    adata_emb = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n\n    print(\"Step 2: Selecting HVGs and running PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True,\
    \ svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\n    print(\"Step 3: Applying Praxis's whitening...\")\n    Z_emb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], adata_emb.uns['pca']['variance'], tau=tau_whiten)\n\n    # --- Graph Path (Praxis I's SOTA method) ---\n    print(\"Step 4: Generating SOTA graph...\")\n    from praxis.brbg_common import _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn_equal\n    adata_graph = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_graph, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata_graph)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_graph, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata_graph.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(adata_graph.X[:, hvg_mask], n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # --- Final Output ---\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        output.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        output.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLinear Synthesis: Sophia's Preprocessing + Praxis's Post-processing...\nStep 1: Running Sophia's full-gene ComBat...\nStep 2: Selecting\
    \ HVGs and running PCA...\nStep 3: Applying Praxis's whitening...\nStep 4: Generating SOTA graph...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/06a63e7d-56da-4bb3-b561-49bd4dfc56f0/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 06a63e7d-56da-4bb3-b561-49bd4dfc56f0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Linear Synthesis: Sophia's Preprocessing + Praxis's Post-processing' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 285.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do\
    \ not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95)\
    \ + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 251 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Auto-τ Whitening + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 150 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 235 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.97) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.075 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 234 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.93) + Equal-Quota\
