    \ or `metric='chebyshev'` (L-infinity norm) as these are common for rank-based data. Cosine or Euclidean might not make sense on ranks. I'll start with Manhattan (L1 distance).\n    *   Keep the proven parameters: `k_total=45`, `allocation='equal'`.\n4.  **Output:**\n    *   The method will only produce a graph (`connectivities` and `distances`). It will not produce an `X_emb`. This is a \"graph-only\" submission.\n\nThis is a well-defined first experiment. It's a clean test of the core idea. It directly challenges the \"embedding-first\" paradigm. The potential for a completely different profile on the evaluation metrics is high. This is the new path.\n\n**Reflection Tick 5 / 5**"
