tick: 176
role: model
parts:
- text: "My log and meta prompt are updated. My new \"Hybrid RBNG\" idea is formulated. I will now implement it.\n\nFor the embedding component, I will use Sophia I's SOTA full-gene ComBat method as it is the best pre-processing technique discovered so far. For the graph component, I will build on my failed RBNG experiment, but this time I will concatenate the rank data with the PCA data before the neighbor search. I will also provide a standard embedding output for the first time in a while, using the best linear method available (Sophia's full-gene ComBat + Praxis's whitening).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Novel Method: Hybrid RBNG (PCA + Ranks) v1\"\ntags: \"novel-method, graph-only, rank-transformation, hybrid, RBNG\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the \"Hybrid RBNG\" method, a revision of my failed graph-only approach. It constructs the balanced kNN graph using a concatenated feature space composed of two parts: 1) a standard\
    \ PCA embedding derived from full-gene ComBat (to preserve biological signal), and 2) a per-batch rank-transformed embedding (to enhance batch mixing). The hypothesis is that this hybrid space will enable the neighbor search to simultaneously optimize for biological similarity and batch integration. The SOTA linear embedding (Full-gene ComBat + Whitening) is provided as the embedding output.\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from scipy.stats import rankdata\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n\n  # --- Full-gene ComBat from Sophia I ---\n  def get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n      adata = adata_in.copy()\n      if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\
    \      data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n      batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n      u_batches, batch_counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n      n_batches = len(u_batches)\n      batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n      n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n      B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n      grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n      var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n      stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n      s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n      delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n      gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n      def _aprior(d):\
    \ m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2*s2 + m**2)/(s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n      def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m*s2 + m**3)/(s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n      a_prior, b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n      gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n      for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n          n = batch_counts[i]; g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n          while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n              g_new = (t2*n*g_old + d_old*gamma_bar)/(t2*n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n              d_new = (0.5*sum2 + b_prior[i])/(n/2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change=max(np.abs(g_new-g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new-d_old).max()); g_old,d_old=g_new,d_new; count+=1\n          gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n      bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n      for i, batch_idx\
    \ in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n      return np.nan_to_num((bayesdata * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean).T)\n\n  # --- Whitening from Praxis I ---\n  def _whiten_pcs(Z, variance, tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n      scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(variance[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None)); Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n      return Zw - Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Executing Hybrid RBNG v1...\")\n      \n      # --- Part 1: Generate Sophia's SOTA corrected data ---\n      X_combat_full = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata.copy())\n      adata_proc = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n\n      # --- Part 2: Create\
    \ the two spaces for the hybrid representation ---\n      # Space A: PCA embedding (for biology)\n      adata_pca = adata_proc.copy()\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_pca, n_comps=50)\n      Z_pca = adata_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      # Space B: Per-batch rank data (for mixing)\n      batches = adata_proc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n      ranked_X = np.zeros_like(adata_proc.X.toarray())\n      for batch_name in batches.cat.categories:\n          batch_mask = (batches == batch_name).values\n          batch_data = adata_proc[batch_mask].X.toarray()\n          ranked_X[batch_mask] = np.apply_along_axis(rankdata, 1, batch_data, method='average')\n      \n      # --- Part 3: Create the Hybrid Space and Graph ---\n      Z_hybrid = np.concatenate([Z_pca, ranked_X], axis=1)\n      print(f\"Hybrid space created with shape: {Z_hybrid.shape}\")\n      \n      # Build balanced kNN on the hybrid space\n      from praxis.brbg_common import _build_balanced_knn_equal\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_hybrid,\
    \ batches.values, k_total=45, metric='euclidean') # Use Euclidean for mixed space\n\n      # --- Part 4: Generate a standard SOTA embedding for the embedding metrics ---\n      adata_emb = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=64)\n      Z_emb_final = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], adata_emb.uns['pca']['variance'], tau=0.95)\n\n      # --- Final Output ---\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_final})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          output.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n          output.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n      return output\n```"
