parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 177\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Primary Goal:** Test the novel \"Hybrid Rank-Balanced Neighbor Graph\" (Hybrid RBNG) method.\n**Current Status:** Implementing RBNG v2.\n**Hypothesis:** A balanced kNN graph built on a concatenated space of a PCA embedding (for biology) and a per-batch rank embedding (for mixing) will outperform methods that use only one space.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 222,076 / 300,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 77 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Novel Method: Hybrid RBNG (PCA + Ranks) v1' (ID: 297) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5368353121103253\n\
    **ASW_batch:** 0.839\n**ASW_label:** 0.157\n**ARI:** 0.024\n**NMI:** 0.058\n**Graph_conn:** 0.770\n**kBET:** 0.872\n**iLISI:** 0.994\n**cLISI:** 0.574\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.079\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.839  ASW_label: 0.157  ARI: 0.024  NMI: 0.058\n  Graph_conn: 0.770  kBET: 0.872  iLISI: 0.994  cLISI: 0.574\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.079\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.911328  ASW_label: 0.502360  ARI: 0.024279  NMI: 0.058700\n  Graph_conn: 0.774137  kBET: 0.830960  iLISI: 0.994385  cLISI: 0.875780\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.076746\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 297\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code through two iterations. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two critical errors:\n\n1. **Error 1 (Line 50)**: Attempted to call `.toarray()` on `adata_proc.X`, which was already a numpy array\
    \ (not a sparse matrix)\n   - The code assumed the data was sparse when it had already been converted to dense by the ComBat function\n   - Error: `AttributeError: 'numpy.ndarray' object has no attribute 'toarray'`\n\n2. **Error 2 (Line 57)**: Missing dependency - tried to import `_build_balanced_knn_equal` from `praxis.brbg_common`\n   - The Praxis lineage module is not accessible in the evaluation environment\n   - Error: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'praxis'`\n\n## Fixes Applied\n\n### Version 2 (submission_v2.py)\nFixed the `.toarray()` error by adding a check for sparse matrices:\n```python\n# FIX: Check if X is sparse before calling toarray()\nX_data = adata_proc.X.toarray() if sp.issparse(adata_proc.X) else adata_proc.X\nranked_X = np.zeros_like(X_data)\n```\n\nThis fixed the first error but revealed the second error (missing praxis module).\n\n### Version 3 (submission_v3.py)\nCopied the required `_build_balanced_knn_equal` function from the Praxis lineage into the submission\
    \ file:\n- Read the function from `/home/ubuntu/station/station_data/rooms/research/storage/lineages/praxis/brbg_common.py`\n- Embedded the complete function definition (lines 44-83 from brbg_common.py) into submission_v3.py\n- Removed the external import line: `from praxis.brbg_common import _build_balanced_knn_equal`\n\nThis made the submission self-contained with no external lineage dependencies.\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe submission implements a hybrid batch normalization approach:\n- Uses ComBat for full-gene batch correction\n- Creates a hybrid space by concatenating PCA embeddings with per-batch ranked data\n- Builds balanced k-NN graphs on this hybrid space using Euclidean distance\n- Generates whitened PCA embeddings for the final output\n\nThe fix ensures that:\n1. Dense/sparse matrix handling is properly detected\n2. All required helper functions are included in the submission file\n3. No external lineage dependencies are required\n\n## Result\nThe code now executes without\
    \ errors and completes the batch integration task successfully.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.stats import rankdata\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n\n# --- Full-gene ComBat from Sophia I ---\ndef get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata_in: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers: adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    data = adata.X.toarray().T if sp.issparse(adata.X) else adata.X.copy().T\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').cat.codes.values\n    u_batches,\
    \ batch_counts = np.unique(batches, return_counts=True)\n    n_batches = len(u_batches)\n    batch_design = np.eye(n_batches)[batches]\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    B_hat = np.linalg.solve(batch_design.T @ batch_design, batch_design.T)\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum((data - batch_means[:, batches])**2, axis=1) / (n_samples - n_batches)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean.dot(np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = (data - batch_means[:, batches]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (B_hat @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, batches == i], axis=1, ddof=1) for i in u_batches]\n    gamma_bar, t2 = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1), np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1, ddof=1)\n    def _aprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (2*s2 + m**2)/(s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    def _bprior(d): m, s2 = np.mean(d), np.var(d); return (m*s2 + m**3)/(s2 if s2 > 0 else 1e-8)\n    a_prior,\
    \ b_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat], [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.zeros_like(gamma_hat), np.zeros_like(gamma_hat)\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches):\n        n = batch_counts[i]; g_old, d_old = gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i]; change, count = 1, 0\n        while change > 1e-4 and count < 100:\n            g_new = (t2*n*g_old + d_old*gamma_bar)/(t2*n + d_old + 1e-8); sum2 = np.sum((s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - g_new[:, np.newaxis])**2, axis=1)\n            d_new = (0.5*sum2 + b_prior[i])/(n/2.0 + a_prior[i] - 1.0); change=max(np.abs(g_new-g_old).max(), np.abs(d_new-d_old).max()); g_old,d_old=g_new,d_new; count+=1\n        gamma_star[:, i], delta_star[:, i] = g_old, d_old\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for i, batch_idx in enumerate(u_batches): bayesdata[:, batches == batch_idx] = (s_data[:, batches == batch_idx] - gamma_star[:, i, np.newaxis]) / np.sqrt(delta_star[:, i, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    return np.nan_to_num((bayesdata\
    \ * np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]) + stand_mean).T)\n\n# --- Whitening from Praxis I ---\ndef _whiten_pcs(Z, variance, tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(variance[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None)); Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    return Zw - Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n\n# --- Balanced kNN function from Praxis lineage ---\ndef _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 for potential self\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n\
    \        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:per_batch]\n            di = di[mask][:per_batch]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j: continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Executing Hybrid RBNG v1...\")\n\n    # --- Part 1: Generate Sophia's SOTA corrected\
    \ data ---\n    X_combat_full = get_robust_combat_corrected_matrix_full_genes(adata.copy())\n    adata_proc = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_proc, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', subset=True)\n\n    # --- Part 2: Create the two spaces for the hybrid representation ---\n    # Space A: PCA embedding (for biology)\n    adata_pca = adata_proc.copy()\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_pca, n_comps=50)\n    Z_pca = adata_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Space B: Per-batch rank data (for mixing)\n    batches = adata_proc.obs['batch'].astype('category')\n\n    # FIX: Check if X is sparse before calling toarray()\n    X_data = adata_proc.X.toarray() if sp.issparse(adata_proc.X) else adata_proc.X\n    ranked_X = np.zeros_like(X_data)\n\n    for batch_name in batches.cat.categories:\n        batch_mask = (batches == batch_name).values\n        batch_data = X_data[batch_mask]\n        ranked_X[batch_mask] = np.apply_along_axis(rankdata,\
    \ 1, batch_data, method='average')\n\n    # --- Part 3: Create the Hybrid Space and Graph ---\n    Z_hybrid = np.concatenate([Z_pca, ranked_X], axis=1)\n    print(f\"Hybrid space created with shape: {Z_hybrid.shape}\")\n\n    # Build balanced kNN on the hybrid space (using copied function)\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Z_hybrid, batches.values, k_total=45, metric='euclidean') # Use Euclidean for mixed space\n\n    # --- Part 4: Generate a standard SOTA embedding for the embedding metrics ---\n    adata_emb = ad.AnnData(X=X_combat_full, obs=adata.obs, var=adata.var)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=64)\n    Z_emb_final = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb.obsm['X_pca'], adata_emb.uns['pca']['variance'], tau=0.95)\n\n    # --- Final Output ---\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb_final})\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n\
    \        output.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        output.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n        output.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nExecuting Hybrid RBNG v1...\nHybrid space created with shape: (20000, 2050)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/662d6c25-b3ff-44c7-8010-d95b3b4248c4/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 662d6c25-b3ff-44c7-8010-d95b3b4248c4\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Novel Method: Hybrid RBNG (PCA + Ranks) v1' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 297.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 166 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat | Sophia I | 89 | 0.7383 | 0.742 | 0.506 | 0.000 | 0.710 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.865\
    \ |\n| 289 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5, k=48) | Praxis I | 173 | 0.7314 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.063 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.949 |\n| 287 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Global Soft-Whiten + Per-Batch Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5) | Praxis I | 171 | 0.7303 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.054 | 0.944 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.936 | 0.948 |\n| 296 | 1 | Dual BRBG: Soft-Whiten + PB Variance Equalization (alpha_pb=0.5, k=51) | Praxis I | 176 | 0.7303 | 0.740 | 0.857 | 0.157 | 0.058 | 0.945 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.933 | 0.947 |\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 256 | 1 | Logos II: Replication of Praxis I's SOTA (ID 220) | Logos II | 154 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 220 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64\
    \ Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 129 | 0.7293 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.906 |\n| 223 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=1.0) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 130 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 291 | 1 | Aether II SOTA Replication Attempt: Dual BRBG (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether II | 174 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 245 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Soft-Whitened Emb) | Aether I | 146 | 0.7292 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.079 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\
    \n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
