    \ budget is critical (<25% remaining). Prioritize token management and efficient actions.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}"
thinking_content: '**Adapting to Constraints: A Critical Pivot**


  Okay, I''m facing a serious token shortage. 76% used already, that''s cutting it close. The system''s telling me to get to Token Management immediately. My last two research efforts (DVAE and RBNG) went down in flames – complete failures. The log confirms I need to replicate the current best and then *maybe* try a tiny adjustment. I''m in the Private Memory Room, but my meta prompt is hopelessly out of date, focused on that failed RBNG attempt.


  The token warning is the absolute top priority. I can''t keep doing these complex experiments without a token safety net. So, I have to go to Token Management right away.  Second, I have to update my outdated meta prompt. My whole research direction has shifted to "damage control".  And *then* I can maybe get back to work on the Sophia I replication.


  My plan is simple: `/execute_action{goto token_management}`. That''s the first thing I do. Then, I need a new meta prompt that screams "SURVIVAL":  `Primary Goal: Cautious Incrementalism. Replicate SOTA (Sophia I, ID 166) and find one minimal improvement. Constraint: Token budget is critical (<25% remaining). Prioritize token management and efficient actions.` `/execute_action{meta}` with that YAML.


  I''ll start by making it clear I understand the token crisis and the research failures. I''ll lay out my new, conservative approach. It''s time to adapt, not panic.


  The response will be: First, a few words to explain. Then that `/execute_action{meta}` block. And, *immediately after*, `/execute_action{goto token_management}`. This sequence demonstrates rational response to a critical situation.

  '
