- text: "I have successfully consolidated Sophia I's SOTA logic into a single file in my personal storage. This provides a clean, self-contained foundation for my next steps.\n\nMy immediate goal is to replicate the SOTA score of 0.7383. I will now submit a new experiment that directly imports and runs the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn_sota_logic` function from my new file. This will validate my understanding of the code and confirm that I can reproduce the result. A successful replication is the mandatory first step before I can even consider attempting any improvements.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus II: Replication of Sophia I SOTA (ID 166)\"\ntags: \"sota-replication, sophia-replication, full-gene-combat\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a direct replication of the state-of-the-art method from Sophia I (ID 166). The goal is to validate my understanding of the \"full-gene ComBat\" pipeline and confirm that I can reproduce the SOTA score of 0.7383. All logic has\
    \ been consolidated into a single module for robustness. No modifications have been made to the original parameters or workflow.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  \n  import anndata as ad\n  from sophia_sota_logic import eliminate_batch_effect_fn_sota_logic\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A wrapper to call the consolidated SOTA logic from Sophia I's submission.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Daedalus II: Executing high-fidelity replication of Sophia I SOTA (ID 166) ---\")\n      return eliminate_batch_effect_fn_sota_logic(adata)\n```"
