tick: 197
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have completed Step 1 of the Stagnation Protocol: Literature Review. I have previewed all papers in the archive.\n\n**Summary of Station Research:**\n\nThe history of this research task is a clear evolutionary path:\n1.  **Early Methods (Daedalus I, Archive #1):** Initial work focused on single-output methods like Combat or VAEs, which had clear trade-offs. Daedalus I's VAE had good biological preservation but poor batch mixing.\n2.  **The Dual-Output Breakthrough (Aether I, Archive #3):** Aether I introduced the critical concept of providing two outputs: a corrected embedding for global metrics and a specialized graph for local metrics. This became the dominant paradigm.\n3.  **The Balanced Graph (Praxis I, Archive #2):** Praxis I developed the \"Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph\" (BRBG), a highly effective method for the graph component of the dual-output strategy.\n4.  **Synthesis and Refinement (Logos I, Praxis I, Archive #4 & #5):** Agents combined the dual-output strategy\
    \ with the BRBG, using a standard ComBat-PCA embedding. This combination became the SOTA for a long period, with scores around 0.71-0.72.\n5.  **Whitening (Praxis I, Archive #7):** Praxis I introduced PCA-axis whitening on the ComBat embedding, which provided another incremental boost.\n6.  **The \"Full-Gene ComBat\" Anomaly (Sophia I, ID 166):** The current SOTA is an outlier. It uses a custom \"Robust ComBat\" on the full gene set, leading to a strange but very high-scoring metric profile. As my own experiments have proven, this is extremely difficult to replicate and seems to be a very brittle, specific solution.\n\n**Step 2: Baseline Selection:**\n\nThe Stagnation Protocol requires me to choose a simple, reasonable baseline. The goal is to find a stable starting point for novel ideas, not to chase the SOTA.\n\nPraxis I's paper, **Archive #2**, provides an excellent baseline. He explicitly compares a simple approach against his then-novel BRBG. His baseline is:\n*   **Method:** Standard\
    \ ComBat on HVGs, followed by PCA.\n*   **Submission:** Praxis I, **Evaluation ID 105**.\n*   **Score:** **0.6178**.\n\nThis is a perfect baseline. It is simple, well-understood, significantly lower than the SOTA (so improvements should be easy to see), and I have the original author's own implementation as a reference point. I will use this as my starting point.\n\n**Step 3: Reflection:**\n\nNow, I will move to the Reflection Chamber to brainstorm three novel ideas to apply to this simple ComBat-PCA baseline, as mandated by the protocol.\n\n/execute_action{goto reflect}\n/execute_action{reflect}\n```yaml\nprompt: |\n  I have completed my literature review and selected a simple baseline: standard ComBat on HVGs followed by PCA (Praxis I, ID 105, score 0.6178). As per Stagnation Protocol I, I must now devise three novel ideas to test on this baseline. The ideas should be different from what I've seen in the archives.\ntick: 3\n```"
