    \ 1. Embed then Correct, 2. Batch-Informed Features, 3. Iterative ComBat.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Stagnation Protocol: Step 3 (Reflection) Complete**\n  *   I have completed the mandated literature review and reflection. I have selected Praxis I's simple ComBat-PCA baseline (ID 105, score 0.6178) as my starting point.\n  *   I have developed three novel ideas to test against this baseline:\n      1.  **\"Embed then Correct\":** Reverse the standard pipeline by running PCA *before* ComBat.\n      2.  **\"Batch-Informed Feature Selection\":** Use batch-discriminative genes instead of HVGs as input for ComBat.\n      3.  **\"Iterative-Refinement ComBat\":** Use an initial ComBat correction to generate pseudo-cell-type clusters, then run a second, more refined ComBat within each cluster.\n\n  **Stagnation Protocol: Step 4 (Experimentation) Beginning**\n  *   My immediate next action is to go to the Research Counter\
    \ and submit a replication of the baseline (ID 105) to ensure I have a stable foundation for my experiments.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Protocol: Baseline Replication (Praxis I, ID 105)\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, baseline, replication, combat, pca\"\nabstract: |\n  As the first part of Stagnation Protocol I, Step 4, this submission aims to faithfully replicate the simple baseline established by Praxis I in evaluation ID 105 (score 0.6178). The method is a standard pipeline of Normalize/Log1p -> Select HVGs -> ComBat -> PCA. This serves as the control against which my three novel ideas will be tested.\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      A faithful replication of the simple baseline from Praxis I, ID 105.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Stagnation Protocol: Reproducing Baseline (Praxis I, ID 105) ---\"\
    )\n      \n      # 1. Normalize and Log1p\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      \n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      \n      # 3. Apply ComBat\n      sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n      \n      # 4. Run PCA\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      \n      # 5. Prepare output\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      adata_out.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      return adata_out\n```"
