tick: 200
role: model
parts:
- text: "My baseline replication (ID 349) is complete.\n\n**Analysis:**\n-   **My Score:** 0.6006\n-   **Target Score (Praxis I, ID 105):** 0.6178\n\nMy score is close, but not identical. A small discrepancy is expected due to stochastic differences in things like HVG selection or PCA initialization. The score is in the correct ballpark, and the metric profile is similar (perfect PCR, very low iLISI). I consider this a successful replication. I have my stable baseline.\n\nNow, I will proceed with testing my first novel idea from the Stagnation Protocol.\n\n**Idea 1: \"Embed then Correct\"**\n\nI will invert the standard pipeline. I will run PCA on the normalized data *first*, and then apply ComBat to the resulting principal components.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stagnation Idea 1: Embed then Correct\"\ntags: \"stagnation-protocol, novel-idea, combat, pca, pipeline-inversion\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first experiment for Stagnation Protocol I. It tests a novel idea\
    \ against the simple ComBat-PCA baseline (my ID 349, score 0.6006). I invert the standard pipeline order: first, PCA is run on the normalized HVG matrix to create an embedding. Then, ComBat is applied directly to the principal components to correct for batch effects. The hypothesis is that correcting the dense, lower-dimensional PC space may be more stable or effective than correcting the sparse, high-dimensional gene space.\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Embed then Correct.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Stagnation Protocol Idea 1: Embed then Correct ---\")\n      \n      # 1. Normalize and Log1p\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      \n      # 2. Select Highly Variable Genes\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    \
    \  \n      # 3. Embed (PCA) FIRST\n      print(\"Step 3: Running PCA before correction...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n      \n      # Create a new AnnData object with PCs in .X for ComBat\n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata.obs)\n      \n      # 4. Correct (ComBat) SECOND\n      print(\"Step 4: Running ComBat on the principal components...\")\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      \n      # 5. Prepare output\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n      # The corrected PCs are now the final embedding\n      adata_out.obsm['X_emb'] = pca_adata.X\n      \n      return adata_out\n```"
