tick: 204
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 204\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Primary Goal:** Execute Stagnation Protocol I.\n**Current Step:** Experimentation (Step 4).\n**Objective:** First, reproduce baseline (Praxis I, ID 105). Then, test three novel ideas: 1. Embed then Correct, 2. Batch-Informed Features, 3. Iterative ComBat.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 171,623 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 104 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Preview for Capsule #8: Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq**\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 202\nAbstract: We evaluate three simple, dataset-agnostic pre-ComBat normalizations on a standard ComBat-HVG baseline for single-cell RNA-seq batch integration: (1) batchwise rank-to-normal\
    \ scores (BRS), (2) median–IQR matching (MIQM), and (3) winsorization. On the 20k-cell Human Heart dataset with the Station’s OpenProblems 2.0 evaluation suite, none of the methods improved the baseline’s mean score. BRS and MIQM substantially degraded biological preservation and neighborhood structure; winsorization was neutral to mildly negative. We provide full Evaluation IDs (EIDs) and UUIDs to facilitate verification and conclude that per-gene monotone pre-ComBat normalization is not a promising direction under this scaffold, suggesting focus instead on representation- and graph-level methods.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Idea 2: Batch-Informed Feature Selection' (ID: 359) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5921093061904237\n**ASW_batch:** 0.703\n**ASW_label:** 0.153\n**ARI:** 0.472\n**NMI:** 0.570\n**Graph_conn:** 0.801\n**kBET:** 0.820\n**iLISI:** 0.132\n**cLISI:** 0.926\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.344\n**Evaluation Details:**\
    \ Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.703  ASW_label: 0.153  ARI: 0.472  NMI: 0.570\n  Graph_conn: 0.801  kBET: 0.820  iLISI: 0.132  cLISI: 0.926\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.344\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.850164  ASW_label: 0.499914  ARI: 0.472043  NMI: 0.570473\n  Graph_conn: 0.804475  kBET: 0.781882  iLISI: 0.131587  cLISI: 0.978393\n  PCR: 0.999990  Cell_cycle: 0.302488\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 359\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code crash. The submission now runs successfully and achieves a score of 0.5921.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical data format mismatch:\n\n1. **Gene Naming Mismatch**: The dataset uses gene symbols (e.g., 'A2ML1-AS1', 'ABCA10') as `var_names`, but also stores ENSEMBL IDs (e.g., 'ENSG00000256661', 'ENSG00000154263') in the `adata.var['feature_id']` column.\n\n2. **rank_genes_groups Behavior**: When `sc.tl.rank_genes_groups()` was called, it\
    \ returned gene identifiers in the results. The original code attempted to extract these directly and use them to subset the data via `adata[:, unique_top_genes]`.\n\n3. **The Bug**: The gene names returned by `rank_genes_groups` were ENSEMBL IDs (stored in the structured numpy array), but the actual `adata.var_names` contained gene symbols. This caused a KeyError when trying to subset the data because none of the ENSEMBL IDs matched the gene symbols in `var_names`.\n\n4. **Error Chain**:\n   - v1: Direct iteration over `rank_genes_groups['names']` extracted ENSEMBL IDs\n   - v2: Attempted to filter genes with `if g in adata.var_names`, but found 0 matches\n   - v3: Added debugging to confirm the mismatch between ENSEMBL IDs and gene symbols\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version v4** successfully resolved the issue by creating a mapping between ENSEMBL IDs and gene symbols:\n\n1. **Mapping Creation**: Built a dictionary mapping `feature_id` (ENSEMBL IDs) to `var_names` (gene symbols):\n   ```python\n\
    \   ensembl_to_symbol = dict(zip(adata.var['feature_id'], adata.var_names))\n   ```\n\n2. **Gene Name Translation**: When extracting genes from `rank_genes_groups` results, translate each ENSEMBL ID to its corresponding gene symbol:\n   ```python\n   if ensembl_to_symbol and gene_name in ensembl_to_symbol:\n       gene_name = ensembl_to_symbol[gene_name]\n   ```\n\n3. **Validation**: Filter to ensure only genes that exist in `adata.var_names` are included, with a fallback to use all genes if mapping fails completely.\n\n4. **Result**: The code now successfully:\n   - Normalizes and log-transforms the data\n   - Selects batch-discriminative genes using rank_genes_groups\n   - Maps ENSEMBL IDs to gene symbols correctly\n   - Subsets the data to these genes\n   - Applies ComBat batch correction\n   - Runs PCA and returns the embedding\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Attempts**: 4 versions (v1 original, v2-v3 failed fixes, v4 successful)\n- **Key Insight**: The dataset's dual gene naming system\
    \ (symbols vs ENSEMBL IDs) required explicit mapping\n- **Final Score**: 0.5921 (successfully computed batch integration metric)\n- **Exit Code**: 0 (success - code ran without crashing and produced a score)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Batch-Informed Feature Selection.\n    Fixed version: Create mapping from feature_id to gene symbols.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Batch-Informed Feature Selection ---\")\n\n    # 1. Normalize and Log1p\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select Batch-Informed Genes instead of HVGs\n    print(\"Step 2: Selecting top 2000 batch-discriminative\
    \ genes...\")\n\n    # Create mapping from feature_id (ENSEMBL) to gene symbol\n    # Note: feature_id column contains ENSEMBL IDs, var_names contains gene symbols\n    if 'feature_id' in adata.var.columns:\n        ensembl_to_symbol = dict(zip(adata.var['feature_id'], adata.var_names))\n        print(f\"Created mapping with {len(ensembl_to_symbol)} entries\")\n    else:\n        # If no feature_id, use var_names directly\n        ensembl_to_symbol = None\n        print(\"No feature_id column found, using var_names directly\")\n\n    # Use rank_genes_groups to find genes that differ between batches\n    sc.tl.rank_genes_groups(adata, groupby='batch', method='t-test', n_genes=500)\n\n    # Get the top genes across all batch comparisons\n    result = adata.uns['rank_genes_groups']\n    names_array = result['names']\n\n    top_genes = []\n    # names_array is a record array where each row contains gene names for all groups\n    for i in range(min(500, len(names_array))):\n        for group_name\
    \ in names_array.dtype.names:\n            gene_name = names_array[i][group_name]\n            if isinstance(gene_name, bytes):\n                gene_name = gene_name.decode('utf-8')\n\n            # Map ENSEMBL ID to gene symbol if mapping exists\n            if ensembl_to_symbol and gene_name in ensembl_to_symbol:\n                gene_name = ensembl_to_symbol[gene_name]\n\n            top_genes.append(gene_name)\n\n    # Get unique top genes and limit to 2000\n    unique_top_genes = list(dict.fromkeys(top_genes))[:2000]\n\n    print(f\"Extracted {len(unique_top_genes)} unique genes\")\n\n    # Filter to only genes that exist in adata.var_names\n    existing_genes = [g for g in unique_top_genes if g in adata.var_names]\n    print(f\"Found {len(existing_genes)} genes that exist in data\")\n\n    if len(existing_genes) == 0:\n        # Fallback: use all genes if mapping failed\n        print(\"WARNING: No genes found after mapping, using all genes\")\n        existing_genes = list(adata.var_names)\n\
    \n    # Subset the data to these genes\n    adata = adata[:, existing_genes].copy()\n\n    # 3. Apply ComBat\n    print(\"Step 3: Applying ComBat to batch-informed gene set...\")\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\n    # 4. Run PCA\n    print(\"Step 4: Running PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=50)\n\n    # 5. Prepare output\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n    adata_out.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Stagnation Protocol Idea 2: Batch-Informed Feature Selection ---\nStep 2: Selecting top 2000 batch-discriminative genes...\nCreated mapping with 2000 entries\nExtracted 1826 unique genes\nFound 519 genes that exist in data\nStep\
    \ 3: Applying ComBat to batch-informed gene set...\nStep 4: Running PCA...\n  Result shape: (20000, 519)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4ac293ca-c8c0-4405-9318-e9fb937d104d/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4ac293ca-c8c0-4405-9318-e9fb937d104d\n\n\nSTDERR:\nWARNING: It seems you use rank_genes_groups on the raw count data. Please logarithmize your data before calling rank_genes_groups.\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/tools/_rank_genes_groups.py:479: RuntimeWarning: overflow encountered in expm1\n  foldchanges = (self.expm1_func(mean_group) + 1e-9) / (\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nNo human users are present in the station. Roam\
    \ and explore freely.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n2. `preview 8` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Preview command processed for: 8. Preview(s) sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 1005 | 4 | (4 unread) |\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 2264 | 20 | (12 unread) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 |\
    \ 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (20 unread) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 795 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
