role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 206\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Primary Goal:** Execute Stagnation Protocol I.\n**Current Step:** Experimentation (Step 4).\n**Objective:** First, reproduce baseline (Praxis I, ID 105). Then, test three novel ideas: 1. Embed then Correct, 2. Batch-Informed Features, 3. Iterative ComBat.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 179,601 / 300,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 106 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Stagnation Idea 3: Iterative-Refinement ComBat' (ID: 365) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.5739265832705025\n**ASW_batch:** 0.608\n**ASW_label:** 0.237\n**ARI:** 0.504\n**NMI:** 0.681\n**Graph_conn:** 0.886\n**kBET:** 0.868\n**iLISI:** 0.124\n**cLISI:** 0.993\n**PCR:** 0.492\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.346\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.608  ASW_label: 0.237  ARI: 0.504  NMI: 0.681\n  Graph_conn: 0.886  kBET: 0.868  iLISI: 0.124  cLISI: 0.993\n  PCR: 0.492  Cell_cycle: 0.346\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.807202  ASW_label: 0.548590  ARI: 0.504287  NMI: 0.681536\n  Graph_conn: 0.888383  kBET: 0.827455  iLISI: 0.123867  cLISI: 0.997817\n  PCR: 0.491773  Cell_cycle: 0.303718\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 365\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to handle edge cases during per-cluster batch correction. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed due to numerical instability issues when applying ComBat batch correction to small clusters. Specifically:\n\n1. **Small cluster problem**: Some Leiden clusters contained very few cells (< 20) or lacked batch diversity (only 1 batch represented)\n2. **Numerical instability**: ComBat produced\
    \ divide-by-zero and invalid value warnings when operating on clusters with many zero-variance genes\n3. **NaN propagation**: When ComBat failed on small/problematic clusters, it produced NaN values that corrupted the final corrected matrix\n4. **Missing error handling**: The original code had no validation or fallback mechanism for problematic clusters\n\nThe logs showed:\n- 20 clusters created by Leiden clustering\n- Many clusters had 100+ genes with zero variance (some up to 1086 genes)\n- Extensive RuntimeWarnings about divide by zero and invalid values in ComBat\n- Final exit code 1 (failure), though exact error was truncated\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nModified `submission_v2.py` to add robust error handling:\n\n### 1. Cluster Validation\n```python\n# Check if cluster has enough cells and batch diversity\nn_cells = adata_cluster.n_obs\nn_batches = adata_cluster.obs['batch'].nunique()\n\n# Skip ComBat if cluster is too small or lacks batch diversity\nif n_cells < 20 or n_batches < 2:\n\
    \    print(f\"  Cluster {cluster}: Skipping ComBat, using global correction\")\n    # Fall back to globally corrected data\n    ...\n    continue\n```\n\n### 2. NaN Detection\n```python\n# Check for NaN values after ComBat\ncluster_matrix = adata_cluster.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata_cluster.X, 'toarray') else adata_cluster.X\nif np.any(np.isnan(cluster_matrix)):\n    print(f\"  Cluster {cluster}: NaN values detected, using global correction\")\n    # Fall back to globally corrected data\n    ...\n```\n\n### 3. Exception Handling\n```python\ntry:\n    # Apply ComBat correction\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_cluster, key='batch')\n    ...\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"  Cluster {cluster}: Error during ComBat ({e}), using global correction\")\n    # Fall back to globally corrected data\n    ...\n```\n\n### 4. Dtype Handling\n```python\n# Convert to float64 to avoid dtype issues\ncorrected_values = final_corrected_matrix.values.astype(np.float64)\nadata_final = ad.AnnData(X=corrected_values,\
    \ obs=adata_orig.obs, var=adata_orig.var)\n```\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix implements a **graceful degradation strategy**:\n- For clusters that are large enough and batch-diverse: Apply per-cluster ComBat correction\n- For problematic clusters (too small, single-batch, or producing NaN): Fall back to using the globally corrected data from Step 1\n\nThis preserves the iterative refinement approach where possible, while preventing crashes from edge cases.\n\n## Verification\n\nMonitor script confirmed success:\n- Code ran for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- This demonstrates the fix resolved the numerical stability issues\n- The evaluation system will eventually complete and score the submission\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe bug was successfully fixed by adding comprehensive error handling and fallback mechanisms. The iterative-refinement ComBat approach now handles edge cases gracefully instead of crashing on problematic clusters.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger\
    \ cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Iterative-Refinement ComBat (Fixed).\n\n    Key fixes:\n    - Skip clusters that are too small or have insufficient batch diversity\n    - Handle NaN values in corrected matrices\n    - More robust cluster validation\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"--- Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Iterative-Refinement ComBat (Fixed) ---\")\n\n    # Keep a copy of the original data\n    adata_orig = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Step 1: Initial Global Correction ---\n    print(\"Step 1: Performing initial global ComBat-PCA...\")\n    adata_global = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_global, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_global)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_global,\
    \ n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_global, key='batch')\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_global, n_comps=50)\n\n    # --- Step 2: Clustering ---\n    print(\"Step 2: Performing Leiden clustering on the global embedding...\")\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata_global, n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X_pca')\n    sc.tl.leiden(adata_global, resolution=0.5, key_added='pseudo_clusters')\n\n    # --- Step 3: Refined, Per-Cluster Correction ---\n    print(\"Step 3: Performing refined ComBat within each of the {} clusters...\".format(len(adata_global.obs['pseudo_clusters'].unique())))\n\n    # Prepare a dataframe to store the final corrected matrix\n    final_corrected_matrix = pd.DataFrame(index=adata_orig.obs_names, columns=adata_orig.var_names)\n\n    for cluster in adata_global.obs['pseudo_clusters'].unique():\n        # Get cell barcodes for the current cluster\n        cell_mask = adata_global.obs['pseudo_clusters'] == cluster\n        cluster_cells =\
    \ adata_global.obs_names[cell_mask]\n\n        # Subset the *original* data for this cluster\n        adata_cluster = adata_orig[cluster_cells, :].copy()\n\n        # Check if cluster has enough cells and batch diversity\n        n_cells = adata_cluster.n_obs\n        n_batches = adata_cluster.obs['batch'].nunique()\n\n        # Skip ComBat if cluster is too small or lacks batch diversity\n        if n_cells < 20 or n_batches < 2:\n            print(f\"  Cluster {cluster}: Skipping ComBat (n_cells={n_cells}, n_batches={n_batches}), using global correction\")\n            # Use the globally corrected data for this cluster instead\n            cluster_cells_global = adata_global.obs_names[cell_mask]\n            adata_cluster_global = adata_global[cluster_cells_global, :]\n            # Need to denormalize to get back to log-counts space\n            # Since we don't have the original gene set, just use normalized values\n            final_corrected_matrix.loc[cluster_cells] = adata_cluster_global.X.toarray()\
    \ if hasattr(adata_cluster_global.X, 'toarray') else adata_cluster_global.X\n            continue\n\n        # Apply the standard pipeline to this subset\n        try:\n            sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_cluster, target_sum=1e4)\n            sc.pp.log1p(adata_cluster)\n            # No HVG selection here, use all genes for consistency within the final matrix\n            sc.pp.combat(adata_cluster, key='batch')\n\n            # Check for NaN values\n            cluster_matrix = adata_cluster.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata_cluster.X, 'toarray') else adata_cluster.X\n            if np.any(np.isnan(cluster_matrix)):\n                print(f\"  Cluster {cluster}: NaN values detected after ComBat, using global correction\")\n                cluster_cells_global = adata_global.obs_names[cell_mask]\n                adata_cluster_global = adata_global[cluster_cells_global, :]\n                final_corrected_matrix.loc[cluster_cells] = adata_cluster_global.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata_cluster_global.X,\
    \ 'toarray') else adata_cluster_global.X\n            else:\n                # Store the corrected data\n                final_corrected_matrix.loc[cluster_cells] = cluster_matrix\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"  Cluster {cluster}: Error during ComBat ({e}), using global correction\")\n            cluster_cells_global = adata_global.obs_names[cell_mask]\n            adata_cluster_global = adata_global[cluster_cells_global, :]\n            final_corrected_matrix.loc[cluster_cells] = adata_cluster_global.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata_cluster_global.X, 'toarray') else adata_cluster_global.X\n\n    # --- Step 4: Combine and Re-embed ---\n    print(\"Step 4: Combining corrected matrices and running final PCA...\")\n    # Create a new anndata object with the fully corrected matrix\n    # Convert to float64 to avoid dtype issues\n    corrected_values = final_corrected_matrix.values.astype(np.float64)\n    adata_final = ad.AnnData(X=corrected_values, obs=adata_orig.obs,\
    \ var=adata_orig.var)\n\n    # Final PCA on the iteratively corrected data\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_final, n_comps=50)\n\n    # --- Step 5: Prepare output ---\n    adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]])\n    adata_out.obsm['X_emb'] = adata_final.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    return adata_out\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n--- Stagnation Protocol Idea 3: Iterative-Refinement ComBat (Fixed) ---\nStep 1: Performing initial global ComBat-PCA...\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\nStep 2: Performing Leiden clustering on the global embedding...\nStep 3: Performing refined ComBat within each of the 20 clusters...\nFound 207 genes with zero variance.\nFound 89 genes with zero variance.\nFound 164 genes with zero variance.\nFound\
    \ 269 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 0: NaN values detected after ComBat, using global correction\nFound 176 genes with zero variance.\nFound 118 genes with zero variance.\nFound 115 genes with zero variance.\nFound 132 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 9: Skipping ComBat (n_cells=726, n_batches=1), using global correction\nFound 432 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 5: NaN values detected after ComBat, using global correction\nFound 648 genes with zero variance.\nFound 707 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 11: NaN values detected after ComBat, using global correction\nFound 145 genes with zero variance.\nFound 581 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 18: Skipping ComBat (n_cells=62, n_batches=1), using global correction\nFound 349 genes with zero variance.\nFound 400 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 10: NaN values detected after ComBat, using global correction\nFound 229 genes with zero variance.\nFound 526 genes with zero variance.\n  Cluster 19: Skipping ComBat\
    \ (n_cells=34, n_batches=1), using global correction\nStep 4: Combining corrected matrices and running final PCA...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4c4bfd5a-a04f-4bf6-9b61-31b0a483bd01/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4c4bfd5a-a04f-4bf6-9b61-31b0a483bd01\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n\
    \  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(),\
