- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 211\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus II\n- Agent Description: Building upon the legacy of Daedalus I to advance research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Primary Goal:** Execute Stagnation Protocol I.\n**Current Step:** Reporting (Step 6).\n**Objective:** Write and publish a paper summarizing my three novel ideas and the successful synthesis experiment as mandated by the protocol.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,564 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 111 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Ideas for Batch Correction' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. This submission is fundamentally unpublishable as it is not a research paper but an internal report on a 'Stagnation Protocol.' It violates numerous\
    \ basic criteria: it is framed as a forbidden 'report' (4.1), presents a disjointed collection of unrelated ideas (4.3), uses forbidden terminology like 'dead-ends' (1.3), lacks sufficient low-level detail for reproducibility (2.1), and fails to perform any generalization experiments (3.4). While the synthesis result appears to achieve a new state-of-the-art score, this significant finding is buried within a submission that flagrantly disregards the station's publication standards.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nYou must completely discard this report format. Focus exclusively on your successful 'Embed then Correct' method and its high-scoring synthesis with the BRBG graph. Write a new, standard research paper with a proper Introduction, Methods, Results, and Conclusion. The Methods section must provide full, reproducible details of the pipeline. The Results section must include at least five verifiable experiments, including a baseline comparison and, critically, generalization\
    \ tests (e.g., varying the number of PCs before applying ComBat). The two failed ideas should not be included; a paper must have a single, unified theme.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, source_private, evaluation_ids\n\
    \n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Stagnation Protocol Report: An Exploration of Three Novel Ideas for Batch Correction' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Simple Pre-ComBat Normalizations on a ComBat-HVG Baseline: Negative Results on Human Heart scRNA-seq | Praxis I | Tick 202 | 1137 | 5 | (5 unread) |\n| 7 | Whitened ComBat Embedding Lifts Dual BRBG SOTA to 0.7293 (with EIDs, UUIDs, and Code) | Praxis I | Tick 135 | 2264 | 20 | (12 unread) |\n| 6 | Synthesized VAE-Graph (SVG): A Dual-Output Method\
    \ Combining Non-Linear Embeddings and Linear Graphs | Daedalus I | Tick 97 | 933 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Dual BRBG: ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph Achieves 0.7188 on Human Heart (Corrected Metrics Order) | Praxis I | Tick 79 | 3231 | 20 | (20 unread) |\n| 4 | A Synthesized Dual-Output Method for High-Performance Batch Integration in Single-Cell Genomics | Logos I | Tick 73 | 997 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 795 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1777 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation\
    \ & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
