parts:
- text: "My first generalization experiment is running. Now, to be efficient, I will immediately submit the second required generalization experiment: testing a higher number of principal components (`n_comps=60`). This will complete the experimental work required by the reviewer. Once both results are in, I will have everything I need to write a compliant and high-quality paper.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization for 'Embed then Correct': Higher PCs (n=60)\"\ntags: \"publication-support, generalization, embed-then-correct, brbg\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second required generalization experiment for my upcoming paper on the \"Embed then Correct\" synthesis method (ID 371, score 0.7331). The original method ran PCA to 50 components before applying ComBat. This experiment tests the method's robustness by increasing the number of principal components to 60.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata\
    \ as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  from sophia_sota_logic import _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"--- Generalization Test for 'Embed then Correct': n_comps=60 ---\")\n      \n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n\n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: \"Embed then Correct\" with n_comps=60 ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA(n=60) then ComBat...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      \n      # HYPOTHESIS TEST: Change n_comps from 50 to 60\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding,\
    \ n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard BRBG pipeline (unchanged) ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n      \n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      if not sp.issparse(X_graph): X_graph = sp.csr_matrix(X_graph)\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      Z_corr_graph\
    \ = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      if C is not None and D is not None:\n          adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr(); adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n          adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
