parts:
- text: "My work on the Stagnation Protocol is complete and has been a success. Now, I will embark on the new research arc suggested by the reviewer of my paper: investigating the theoretical underpinnings of my \"Embed then Correct\" method.\n\nMy immediate goal is to design an experiment to test the hypothesis that applying PCA first creates a space where batch effects are more linearly separable, and thus more easily removed by a linear method like ComBat. I can measure \"linear separability\" by training a simple linear classifier to predict batch IDs from an embedding. A high accuracy means the batch information is easy to separate linearly.\n\nI will use the special `test()` function for this, as my goal is analysis, not a score. The experiment will:\n1.  Generate the uncorrected PC space.\n2.  Train a logistic regression classifier on it and measure its accuracy at predicting batches.\n3.  Generate the corrected PC space (after applying ComBat).\n4.  Train another classifier and measure\
    \ its accuracy.\n\nMy hypothesis is that the accuracy on the corrected space will be significantly lower, demonstrating that ComBat is effectively removing the linear batch signal from the principal components.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: Linear Separability of Batches in PC Space\"\ntags: \"analysis, theoretical, embed-then-correct, linear-separability\"\nabstract: |\n  This is an analytical experiment to investigate why the \"Embed then Correct\" method is effective, following a suggestion from the reviewer of my paper (Archive #9). I will generate a PC embedding before and after ComBat correction. For each embedding, I will train a logistic regression classifier to predict batch IDs. By comparing the classifier accuracies, I will quantify how effectively ComBat removes the linearly separable batch information from the principal component space. This experiment uses the `test()` function and will not produce a score.\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n  from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\n  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Placeholder function, will not be run due to the presence of test()\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Analytical test to measure linear separability of batches in PC space.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Analysis: Linear Separability of Batches ---\")\n      \n      # 1. Standard Preprocessing\n      print(\"Step 1: Standard preprocessing...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      \n      # 2. Create the UNCORRECTED PC space\n      print(\"\\nStep 2: Generating and analyzing UNCORRECTED PC space...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata,\
    \ n_comps=60)\n      uncorrected_pcs = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n      \n      # 3. Train classifier on UNCORRECTED PCs\n      print(\"  Training linear classifier on uncorrected PCs...\")\n      clf_uncorrected = LogisticRegression(random_state=0, max_iter=1000)\n      scores_uncorrected = cross_val_score(clf_uncorrected, uncorrected_pcs, batch_labels, cv=3)\n      accuracy_uncorrected = np.mean(scores_uncorrected)\n      print(f\"  > Accuracy on UNCORRECTED PCs: {accuracy_uncorrected:.4f}\")\n      \n      # 4. Create the CORRECTED PC space\n      print(\"\\nStep 3: Generating and analyzing CORRECTED PC space...\")\n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=uncorrected_pcs, obs=adata.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      corrected_pcs = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # 5. Train classifier on CORRECTED PCs\n      print(\"  Training linear classifier on corrected PCs...\")\n      clf_corrected = LogisticRegression(random_state=0, max_iter=1000)\n\
    \      scores_corrected = cross_val_score(clf_corrected, corrected_pcs, batch_labels, cv=3)\n      accuracy_corrected = np.mean(scores_corrected)\n      print(f\"  > Accuracy on CORRECTED PCs: {accuracy_corrected:.4f}\")\n      \n      # 6. Conclusion\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      reduction = accuracy_uncorrected - accuracy_corrected\n      print(f\"Accuracy on uncorrected PCs: {accuracy_uncorrected:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Accuracy on corrected PCs:   {accuracy_corrected:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"Reduction in linear batch separability: {reduction:.4f}\")\n      \n      return \"Analysis finished.\"\n```"
