tick: 222
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully pruned my history, bringing my token usage down to 70%. I am on cooldown for further pruning, which is acceptable.\n\nMy next step is to fix the bug in my analytical experiment and resubmit it. The error was calling `.toarray()` on a dense numpy array. I will remove the redundant `.toarray()` call.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors (v2)\"\ntags: \"analysis, theoretical, embed-then-correct, combat, bug-fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a resubmission of my second analytical experiment, which failed due to a simple coding error (`.toarray()` called on a dense array). The scientific goal is unchanged: to test the hypothesis that ComBat's estimates are more stable in the dense, low-dimensional PC space by comparing the statistical properties of the correction vectors it learns in both the gene space and the PC space.\ncontent: |\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\
    \  import numpy as np\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Placeholder function, will not be run due to the presence of test()\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Analytical test to compare the stability of ComBat correction vectors.\n      Version 2: Fixes the .toarray() bug.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Analysis: Stability of ComBat Correction Vectors (v2) ---\")\n      \n      # --- Pipeline 1: Standard 'Correct then Embed' ---\n      print(\"\\n--- Pipeline 1: Correct then Embed ---\")\n      adata_c_e = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_c_e, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_c_e)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_c_e, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      \n      pre_combat_gene_space = adata_c_e.X.toarray().copy()\n      \n      sc.pp.combat(adata_c_e, key='batch')\n      # *** THE CRITICAL FIX ***\n      # sc.pp.combat\
    \ converts .X to a dense numpy array in-place. No .toarray() needed.\n      post_combat_gene_space = adata_c_e.X.copy()\n      \n      batch_mask = (adata_c_e.obs['batch'] == adata_c_e.obs['batch'].cat.categories[0])\n      correction_vector_gene_space = np.mean(post_combat_gene_space[batch_mask, :] - pre_combat_gene_space[batch_mask, :], axis=0)\n      \n      print(\"Analysis of correction vector in GENE space:\")\n      print(f\"  > Mean magnitude:   {np.mean(np.abs(correction_vector_gene_space)):.6f}\")\n      print(f\"  > Std Dev of mags:  {np.std(np.abs(correction_vector_gene_space)):.6f}\")\n      print(f\"  > Max magnitude:    {np.max(np.abs(correction_vector_gene_space)):.6f}\")\n\n      # --- Pipeline 2: Novel 'Embed then Correct' ---\n      print(\"\\n--- Pipeline 2: Embed then Correct ---\")\n      adata_e_c = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_e_c, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_e_c)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_e_c, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch',\
    \ flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      \n      sc.pp.pca(adata_e_c, n_comps=60)\n      pre_combat_pc_space = adata_e_c.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=pre_combat_pc_space, obs=adata_e_c.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      post_combat_pc_space = pca_adata.X.copy()\n\n      batch_mask_pc = (pca_adata.obs['batch'] == pca_adata.obs['batch'].cat.categories[0])\n      correction_vector_pc_space = np.mean(post_combat_pc_space[batch_mask_pc, :] - pre_combat_pc_space[batch_mask_pc, :], axis=0)\n\n      print(\"Analysis of correction vector in PC space:\")\n      print(f\"  > Mean magnitude:   {np.mean(np.abs(correction_vector_pc_space)):.6f}\")\n      print(f\"  > Std Dev of mags:  {np.std(np.abs(correction_vector_pc_space)):.6f}\")\n      print(f\"  > Max magnitude:    {np.max(np.abs(correction_vector_pc_space)):.6f}\")\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      return \"Analysis finished.\"\n```"
