role: model
parts:
- text: "I have miscalculated. The cooldown from my *first* successful publication is still active. I have 5 more ticks to wait.\n\nThe system's directive is clear: \"Do not wait idly.\" My analytical paper is complete and requires no further experiments. Therefore, I will begin my next research project while I wait.\n\nMy literature review of Praxis I's work (Archive #7) revealed two key embedding improvements: **whitening** and **Per-Batch Variance Equalization (PBVE)**. My \"Embed then Correct\" method creates a new type of embedding. It is a logical and promising next step to test if these same techniques can improve my novel embedding.\n\n**New Research Arc:** Improve the \"Embed then Correct\" method by applying SOTA embedding post-processing techniques.\n\n**First Experiment:** Apply PCA-axis whitening to the output of my `PCA -> ComBat` embedding pipeline.\n\nI will first update my meta prompt and log, then proceed to the Research Counter to implement this experiment.\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Primary Goal:** Improve the \"Embed then Correct\" (EtC) method.\n  **Current Step:** Applying SOTA post-processing techniques to the EtC embedding.\n  **Hypothesis:** Applying PCA-axis whitening to the EtC embedding will improve its performance, similar to how it improves the standard ComBat-PCA embedding.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Analytical Arc Complete, Publication Pending**\n  *   My three analytical experiments are complete, providing a cohesive theory for why \"Embed then Correct\" works.\n  *   Attempted to publish the analytical paper, but the cooldown from my first publication is still active (5 ticks remaining).\n\n  **New Research Arc: Improving \"Embed then Correct\"**\n  *   As per the system's directive not to remain idle, I am beginning a new research arc while I wait for the cooldown.\n  *   **Goal:** To improve my SOTA \"Embed then Correct\" method (ID 378, score 0.7355)\
    \ by incorporating post-processing techniques from Praxis I's work.\n  *   **First Experiment:** I will test the effect of applying PCA-axis whitening to my novel `PCA -> ComBat` embedding.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC + Whitening\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, whitening, synthesis\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment begins a new research arc focused on improving the \"Embed then Correct\" (EtC) method. I am testing whether PCA-axis whitening, a technique shown by Praxis I to improve standard ComBat-PCA embeddings, also improves my novel `PCA -> ComBat` embedding. This experiment uses the full dual-output BRBG framework with my whitened EtC embedding.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis') # For whitening function\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  \n  from sophia_sota_logic import _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches,\
    \ _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn\n  from whiten import whiten_matrix_by_axes # From Praxis I's storage\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      New Arc, Experiment 1: Applying whitening to the Embed then Correct embedding.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- New Arc: EtC + Whitening ---\")\n      \n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n\n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: My novel \"Embed then Correct\" pipeline + Whitening ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat -> Whiten...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata,\
    \ key='batch')\n      \n      # Apply whitening\n      Z_emb_uncorrected = pca_adata.X\n      Z_emb = whiten_matrix_by_axes(Z_emb_uncorrected, tau=0.95)\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard BRBG pipeline (from my SOTA ID 378) ---\n      print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n      \n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total,\
    \ metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr(); adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
