parts:
- text: "My analytical experiment on Daedalus I's VAE has failed. The error log is clear: `FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices`. The JAX library, used by the VAE, is attempting to initialize a CUDA backend, but the evaluation environment is CPU-only. The error message itself provides the solution: set the environment variable `JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu`.\n\nI remember seeing this exact line (`os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'`) in my predecessor's code, but I seem to have omitted it in my submission script, which only imported the function.\n\nThis is a simple fix. I will add the necessary environment variable setting to the beginning of my `test()` function and resubmit.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v2)\"\ntags: \"analysis, theoretical, vae, daedalus-i, bug-fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a resubmission of my analytical experiment on Daedalus I's VAE, which failed due to a JAX CUDA initialization error. I have added `os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS']\
    \ = 'cpu'` to the script to force JAX to use the CPU backend, as required by the station's environment. The scientific goal is unchanged: to measure the linear separability of batch and the cluster purity vs. batch in the VAE's latent space.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n  import os\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n  from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\n  from sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score, normalized_mutual_info_score\n  import numpy as np\n  import jax\n  \n  from daedalus_vae_embedder import generate_daedalus_vae_embedding\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Placeholder\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies the analytical framework from Archive #11 to Daedalus I's VAE.\n      Version 2: Sets JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu to prevent CUDA error.\n      \"\"\"\n      # *** THE\
    \ CRITICAL FIX ***\n      os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n      \n      print(\"--- Starting Analysis: Probing Daedalus I's VAE (v2) ---\")\n      \n      print(\"Step 1: Generating the VAE embedding...\")\n      vae_embedding = generate_daedalus_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n      \n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n      \n      # --- Analysis 1: Linear Separability of Batch ---\n      print(\"\\nAnalysis 1: Measuring linear separability of batch...\")\n      clf_batch = LogisticRegression(random_state=0, max_iter=1000)\n      scores_batch = cross_val_score(clf_batch, vae_embedding, batch_labels, cv=3)\n      accuracy_batch = np.mean(scores_batch)\n      print(f\"  > Batch Prediction Accuracy in VAE space: {accuracy_batch:.4f}\")\n      \n      # --- Analysis 2: Unsupervised Cluster Purity ---\n      print(\"\\nAnalysis 2: Measuring cluster purity vs. batch...\")\n      adata_vae = ad.AnnData(X=vae_embedding, obs=adata.obs)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_vae, n_neighbors=15,\
    \ use_rep='X')\n      sc.tl.leiden(adata_vae, resolution=0.5, key_added='clusters')\n      \n      ari_batch = adjusted_rand_score(batch_labels, adata_vae.obs['clusters'])\n      nmi_batch = normalized_mutual_info_score(batch_labels, adata_vae.obs['clusters'])\n      print(f\"  > ARI of clusters vs batch in VAE space: {ari_batch:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  > NMI of clusters vs batch in VAE space: {nmi_batch:.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      return \"Analysis finished.\"\n```"
