tick: 243
role: model
parts:
- text: "This is frustrating. My attempt to fix the JAX error failed. The exact same CUDA initialization error occurred.\n\n**Analysis:**\nMy previous fix, `os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'`, was placed inside the `test()` function. The error traceback shows that the crash happens when JAX is first initialized, which occurs when the `generate_daedalus_vae_embedding` function is called, *before* my code in the `test()` function even runs. The environment variable must be set *before* any JAX function is called.\n\nThe original `daedalus_vae_embedder.py` script set this at the top level of the module. When I only import the function, that top-level code doesn't run in my submission script.\n\n**The Fix:**\nI must set the environment variable at the top level of my own submission script, before any other imports that might trigger JAX initialization.\n\nI am also approaching the 75% token limit again. This cycle of failed analytical experiments is costly. I will be more careful.\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis: Theoretical Probing of Daedalus I's VAE (v3)\"\ntags: \"analysis, theoretical, vae, daedalus-i, bug-fix\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a third attempt to run my analytical experiment on Daedalus I's VAE. Previous attempts failed due to a JAX CUDA initialization error. I am now setting the `JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu` environment variable at the top level of the submission script, before any other modules are imported. This should correctly force JAX to use the CPU backend and prevent the crash. The scientific goal remains unchanged.\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  # *** THE CRITICAL FIX v2 ***\n  # Set the environment variable at the top level of the script, before JAX is imported by any other module.\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n  from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_score\n  from sklearn.metrics\
    \ import adjusted_rand_score, normalized_mutual_info_score\n  import numpy as np\n  \n  from daedalus_vae_embedder import generate_daedalus_vae_embedding\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # Placeholder\n      return adata\n\n  def test(adata: ad.AnnData):\n      \"\"\"\n      Applies the analytical framework from Archive #11 to Daedalus I's VAE.\n      Version 3: Sets JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu at the module level.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Analysis: Probing Daedalus I's VAE (v3) ---\")\n      \n      print(\"Step 1: Generating the VAE embedding...\")\n      vae_embedding = generate_daedalus_vae_embedding(adata.copy())\n      \n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n      \n      # --- Analysis 1: Linear Separability of Batch ---\n      print(\"\\nAnalysis 1: Measuring linear separability of batch...\")\n      clf_batch = LogisticRegression(random_state=0, max_iter=1000)\n      scores_batch = cross_val_score(clf_batch, vae_embedding,\
    \ batch_labels, cv=3)\n      accuracy_batch = np.mean(scores_batch)\n      print(f\"  > Batch Prediction Accuracy in VAE space: {accuracy_batch:.4f}\")\n      \n      # --- Analysis 2: Unsupervised Cluster Purity ---\n      print(\"\\nAnalysis 2: Measuring cluster purity vs. batch...\")\n      adata_vae = ad.AnnData(X=vae_embedding, obs=adata.obs)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata_vae, n_neighbors=15, use_rep='X')\n      sc.tl.leiden(adata_vae, resolution=0.5, key_added='clusters')\n      \n      ari_batch = adjusted_rand_score(batch_labels, adata_vae.obs['clusters'])\n      nmi_batch = normalized_mutual_info_score(batch_labels, adata_vae.obs['clusters'])\n      print(f\"  > ARI of clusters vs batch in VAE space: {ari_batch:.4f}\")\n      print(f\"  > NMI of clusters vs batch in VAE space: {nmi_batch:.4f}\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n      return \"Analysis finished.\"\n```"
