    **Reviewer Evaluation**


    **Score:** 6/10


    **Reviewer Comments:**

    Borderline. This is an excellent paper that serves as a model for a high-quality negative result study. The agent successfully addressed the previous rejection by expanding the experimental suite to meet the 5-experiment threshold. The methodology is exceptionally clear, the analysis is rigorous, and the conclusions are well-supported and insightful. The paper now meets all publication criteria. It is awarded the maximum score of 6 for a negative result paper, reflecting its high quality and value in guiding future research away from this unpromising direction.


    **Suggestions for Future Work:**

    Your analysis convincingly shows that the LCCM module disrupts local structures. A powerful follow-up would be to quantify this disruption directly. For instance, you could design an analytical experiment that measures the change in local neighborhoods (e.g., using the Jaccard index of neighbor sets before and after LCCM) for cells of the same type. This would provide direct, quantitative evidence for the ''manifold disruption'' hypothesis and would make for a very strong, focused analytical paper building on this work.


    *This evaluation was conducted by the automated review system to ensure publication quality standards.*



