tick: 255
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully pruned my history and read Sophia II's new paper.\n\n**Analysis of Archive #13:**\n-   Sophia II investigated a novel post-processing step called \"Latent Correlation Minimization\" (LCCM).\n-   The core idea was to use a neural network to explicitly decorrelate the embedding from the batch labels.\n-   The result was a strong **negative**. While PCR was maintained, local mixing metrics (`ASW_batch`, `iLISI`) were consistently and severely degraded, even when trying to preserve the original structure.\n-   **Key Insight:** This is another example, like my own failed \"Cross-Batch Stitching\", where a seemingly logical idea to improve one aspect of the integration (linear decorrelation or graph connectivity) ends up disrupting the delicate local manifold structure, harming the overall result. This reinforces the idea that the local neighborhood structure is extremely sensitive.\n\nMy immediate path is now clear. I have my token budget under control, and I have\
    \ surveyed the latest research. My planned experiment, tuning the `gamma_max` of the adaptive residualization, is still the most logical next step. It is a direct attempt to optimize a promising method, and it is unrelated to the failed LCCM approach.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"EtC + Adaptive Residualization (gamma_max=0.72)\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, adaptive-residualization, hyperparameter-tuning\"\nabstract: |\n  My previous experiment (ID 437) successfully used 'adaptive per-PC residualization' to improve graph metrics but slightly harmed biological preservation. This experiment tunes the adaptive rule to be less aggressive. I am reducing `gamma_max` from 0.74 to 0.72, hypothesizing that this will retain the graph improvements while recovering the small loss in ARI/NMI, potentially leading to a new SOTA score. This is a resubmission of a previously failed action due to being in the wrong room.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\
    \n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n  from sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\n  from sklearn.linear_model import Ridge\n\n  from sophia_sota_logic import _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _build_balanced_knn\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n      model = Ridge(alpha=l2, fit_intercept=False, random_state=0)\n      model.fit(B, Z)\n      Z_hat = model.predict(B)\n      ss_res = np.sum((Z - Z_hat)**2, axis=0)\n      ss_tot = np.sum((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2, axis=0)\n      # Clamp to avoid division by zero or negative R^2\n      r2_per_pc = 1 - ss_res / np.maximum(ss_tot, 1e-12)\n      return Z_hat, np.maximum(0, r2_per_pc)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Tuning Experiment: Reducing gamma_max in adaptive residualization.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Tuning: EtC + Adaptive Residualization (gamma_max=0.72) ---\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING\
    \ PATH ---\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      Z_emb = pca_adata.X\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: ADAPTIVE BRBG pipeline ---\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      # *** HYPOTHESIS TEST: gamma_max = 0.72 ***\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma_max=0.72; lam=0.9; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      \n      Z_hat, r2_per_pc = _ridge_batch_fit_predict_per_pc(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      gamma_per_pc = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2_per_pc)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - (gamma_per_pc * Z_hat)\n      \n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr(); adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
