tick: 257
role: model
parts:
- text: "The results for my `gamma_max=0.72` experiment are in.\n\n**Analysis of ID 443:**\n-   **Score:** 0.7338\n-   **Comparison:**\n    -   `gamma_max=0.74` (ID 437): 0.7341\n    -   My SOTA (ID 378): 0.7355\n-   **Result:** **Failure.** The score is slightly lower than the previous experiment and still below my SOTA. The metrics are nearly identical, indicating this small change had a negligible negative effect.\n\n**Conclusion:**\nMy attempt to optimize the \"Adaptive Residualization\" method by tuning `gamma_max` has not yielded an improvement. It seems the original `gamma_max=0.74` is a robust local optimum. While the adaptive method successfully improves the graph metrics as a proof of concept, it does not seem to be a path to a new SOTA score in its current form.\n\nThis research arc is now complete. I have tested my three novel ideas from reflection.\n1.  **Local-Aware Stitching:** Failure.\n2.  **Adaptive Residualization:** Validated the mechanism, but did not improve SOTA. Failure.\n\
    3.  **Hybrid Embedding Space:** Untested.\n\nGiven the diminishing returns and my dwindling time, I will not pursue the \"Hybrid Embedding Space\" idea, which is the most radical and likely to fail. My focus must be on producing a final, high-quality contribution.\n\n**Final Plan:**\nI have achieved a high score of 0.7355, very close to the station SOTA. I have published two papers. My most significant contribution remains the \"Embed then Correct\" method. I will now perform my final duty as a researcher: I will attempt to synthesize my best method with the absolute SOTA to see if a final breakthrough is possible. The SOTA method (Praxis I, Sophia I) uses a `Whitening + PBVE` step on the embedding. I will apply this to my `EtC` embedding.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Synthesis: EtC + Whitening + PBVE\"\ntags: \"embed-then-correct, whitening, pbve, synthesis, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This is my final experiment, an attempt to synthesize my best method with\
    \ the station's SOTA techniques. I will take my high-performing \"Embed then Correct\" (EtC) embedding and apply the two key post-processing steps from Praxis I's SOTA: PCA-axis whitening and Per-Batch Variance Equalization (PBVE). This is a direct test to see if these state-of-the-art embedding refinements are compatible with and can elevate the EtC pipeline to a new SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\n  sys.path.append('storage/Daedalus')\n\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  import numpy as np\n\n  from sophia_sota_logic import _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd, _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict, _build_balanced_knn\n  from whiten import whiten_matrix_by_axes\n  from perbatch_var_equalization import per_batch_variance_equalization_matrix\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Final experiment: Synthesizing EtC with SOTA post-processing.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"---\
    \ Final Synthesis: EtC + Whitening + PBVE ---\")\n      \n      # --- EMBEDDING PATH: EtC + SOTA Post-processing ---\n      print(\"Embedding Path: Running PCA -> ComBat -> Whiten -> PBVE...\")\n      adata_for_embedding = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_embedding, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_embedding)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_for_embedding, n_top_genes=2000, batch_key='batch', flavor='seurat_v3', subset=True)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_for_embedding, n_comps=60)\n      \n      pca_adata = ad.AnnData(X=adata_for_embedding.obsm['X_pca'], obs=adata_for_embedding.obs)\n      sc.pp.combat(pca_adata, key='batch')\n      \n      # Apply SOTA post-processing\n      Z_emb_combat = pca_adata.X\n      Z_emb_whiten = whiten_matrix_by_axes(Z_emb_combat, tau=0.95)\n      Z_emb = per_batch_variance_equalization_matrix(Z_emb_whiten, pca_adata.obs['batch'].values, alpha=0.5)\n      \n      # --- GRAPH PATH: Standard BRBG (from my SOTA ID 378) ---\n \
    \     print(\"Graph Path: Running standard BRBG...\")\n      adata_for_graph = adata.copy()\n      n_pcs_graph=50; gamma=0.74; l2=1e-3; k_total=48; metric='cosine'; random_state=0\n      \n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_for_graph, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_for_graph)\n      hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_for_graph)\n      X_graph = adata_for_graph.X[:, hvg_mask]\n      Z_graph = _pca_truncated_svd(X_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n      \n      batches = np.asarray(adata_for_graph.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n      B_onehot, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_onehot, Z_graph, l2=l2)\n      Z_corr_graph = Z_graph - gamma * Z_hat\n      C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr_graph, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n      \n      # --- Final Output ---\n      adata_out = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': Z_emb})\n      adata_out.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr();\
    \ adata_out.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n      adata_out.uns['neighbors'] = {'connectivities_key': 'connectivities', 'distances_key': 'distances'}\n          \n      return adata_out\n```"
